{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5f1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06ed9-7c63-74b3-b8db-139ac4482e30"},"sequence":339,"recorded_at":1780531400000673,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"680c30af-893a-4c96-ab8b-878d612e53c6","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"680c30af-893a-4c96-ab8b-878d612e53c6","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"680c30af-893a-4c96-ab8b-878d612e53c6"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"a5b3b663-0a33-47cd-a3e1-69ff06741390"},"task_id":"a5b3b663-0a33-47cd-a3e1-69ff06741390","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"a5b3b663-0a33-47cd-a3e1-69ff06741390","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-2890sd/TASK-260830-2890sd_review-verdict-rev4.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-2890sd — review round 3 verdict\n2|\n3|**Verdict: changes requested → `to-dev`.**\n4|\n5|Reviewed: worktree `.temp/STORY-260830-3jqsx1/worktree`, branch\n6|`task-board/story/STORY-260830-3jqsx1`, HEAD `44a4699` (round-2 rework;\n7|`d8fc669` beneath it). Repo-wide `go test ./...` green, `go build ./...` clean,\n8|`go vet ./internal/provider` clean. Working tree restored and verified clean\n9|after every mutant (`git status --short` empty).\n10|\n11|## 0. The empty `repository_delta`\n12|\n13|`CR-TASK-260830-2890sd-4` reports `repository_delta=empty`: base OID\n14|`44a4699` == candidate tree `4427790` == `HEAD^{tree}`. This is a\n15|CR-construction artifact, not a producer that changed nothing. The round-2\n16|rework **is** `44a4699` (+510 lines: `owner_root_test.go`,\n17|`digest_sweep_test.go`, `source_inventory_test.go`, `discovery_test.go`,\n18|`LOGBOOK.md`); the CR base was snapshotted at that commit instead of at the\n19|pre-rework checkpoint `d8fc669`, so the reviewable delta collapsed to nothing.\n20|I reviewed `git diff d8fc669..44a4699` plus the whole of `internal/provider`\n21|rather than the empty patch. **Verdict note for the orchestrator: the\n22|checkpoint that produced this CR is stale by one commit — the same\n23|`checkpoint_oid`-behind-leaf shape this story has hit before. Fix the\n24|checkpoint before the next CR; the review itself was not blocked by it.**\n25|\n26|## 1. Round-2 findings F6–F10: confirmed closed\n27|\n28|Confirmed cheaply with my own mutants, per the brief. All four are genuinely\n29|closed, not re-declared.\n30|\n31|| Finding | Mutant | Result |\n32|| --- | --- | --- |\n33|| F6 uid 0 admitted | `if uid == 0 { return true }` in `OwnerPolicy.Approves` | killed — `TestOwnerPolicyTreatsRootWithoutException` |\n34|| F7 abs-path gate at index 0 only | gate wrapped in `&& index == 0` (both `plugin_dirs` and `PATH`) | killed — `TestDiscoverRefusesRelativePluginDir`, `TestDiscoverRefusesRelativePATHDir` |\n35|| F8 two LOGBOOK entries unlanded | `git show 44a4699 --name-only` | landed, 21 lines |\n36|| F9 ratio compared a literal to itself | fourth production source site added to `Discover` | killed — `TestTrustGateSourceInventoryIsDerivedFromDiscover` |\n37|| F10 digest gate on a prefix | `sum[:1]` and `sum[31:]` comparisons | killed — `TestVerifyRefusesDigestChangeAtEveryByteIndex` (32/32 sweep) |\n38|\n39|## 2. G-A — does the derivation fail closed on an empty domain?\n40|\n41|**For `source_inventory_test.go`: yes.** Five mutants, five kills.\n42|\n43|| # | Mutant on the derivation / production | Result | Killed by |\n44|| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n45|| A1 | `deriveDiscoverSourceSites` returns `discoverSourceSites{}` | killed | `inlineBuiltins = 0, want exactly 1` |\n46|| A2 | derivation truncates `collectClasses` to 1 of 2 real sites | killed | `1 collectDirectory sites [plugin_dirs], want exactly 2` |\n47|| A3 | production bypass source: direct `ReadDir` + `externalID` + inline `KindExternal` in `Discover` | killed | `reads 1 directories outside collectDirectory` |\n48|| A4 | inline `KindExternal` candidate only (no `ReadDir`) | killed | `builds 1 external candidates outside trustCandidate` + 6 behavioural tests |\n49|| A5 | direct `externalID` call in `Discover` only | killed | `parses 1 executable names outside collectDirectory` |\n50|\n51|The exact-count assertions (`inlineBuiltins != 1`, `len(collectClasses) != 2`,\n52|the sorted-label equality) are the floor: an empty or short derivation cannot\n53|pass. Each of the three zero-expected counters (`directReads`,\n54|`directNameParses`, `inlineExternals`) is individually live — A3/A4/A5 each\n55|redden a different one. An unreadable or unparseable `provider.go`, and a\n56|missing `func Discover`, are `t.Fatalf`/`t.Fatal`. **G-A is answered for the\n57|inventory it was asked about.**\n58|\n59|**But the same question, asked of the package's other derived domains, finds\n60|one that answers no — see F11.**\n61|\n62|## 3. G-B — forced traversal of every gate in `internal/provider`\n63|\n64|Discovered by walking the production source (`provider.go`, `os.go`,\n65|`os_unix.go`, `os_windows.go`), not by recalling earlier rounds. Every row was\n66|attacked with at least one mutant; narrowing mutants were preferred over\n67|deletion where the gate has a class to narrow.\n68|\n69|**Buckets:** `full` = a narrowing mutant reddens; `partial` = narrowing\n70|reddens but deletion or a neighbouring form survives; `sliver` = the gate is\n71|tested on one point of its domain only; `unevidenced` = no mutant on it\n72|reddens anything.\n73|\n74|### Discover / configuration\n75|\n76|| # | Gate | Mutant | Result | Bucket |\n77|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n78|| 1 | `plugin_dirs[i]` absolute-path refusal | narrowed to `index == 0`; deleted | killed | full |\n79|| 2 | `PATH[i]` absolute-path refusal | narrowed to `index == 0` | killed | full |\n80|| 3 | `allow_path_plugins` gate | `if true` (PATH always scanned) | killed | full |\n81|| 4 | duplicate-ID refusal | narrowed to same-source; byte-identical override added | killed | full |\n82|| 5 | source enumeration order | builtins hoisted above `plugin_dirs` | killed | full |\n83|| 6 | builtin registry contents / order | dropped `pi`; swapped `codex`/`claude` | killed | full |\n84|| 7 | bytewise entry sort within a directory | `sort.Strings` removed | killed | full |\n85|| 8 | `Discover` returns no partial set with a refusal | `return nil, err` → `return out, err` | **SURVIVED** | **unevidenced** |\n86|| 9 | `Builtins()` returns a copy | returns `builtinOrder` directly | **SURVIVED** | **unevidenced** |\n87|\n88|### Executable name grammar\n89|\n90|| # | Gate | Mutant | Result | Bucket |\n91|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n92|| 10 | `ExecutablePrefix` constant value | loosened to `\"ax-\"` | killed | full |\n93|| 11 | prefix is an **anchor**, not a substring | `strings.CutPrefix` → `strings.Cut` | **SURVIVED** | **sliver** |\n94|| 12 | provider-id grammar refusal | malformed name skipped; malformed name accepted | killed | full |\n95|\n96|### `trustCandidate`\n97|\n98|| # | Gate | Mutant | Result | Bucket |\n99|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n100|| 13 | `ReadDir` failure → `local_precondition_failed` | error swallowed as empty directory | killed | full |\n101|| 14 | `Canonicalize` failure → precondition | narrowed to `/opt` prefix | killed | partial |\n102|| 14b | same, deletion form | `canon = path` on error | **SURVIVED** | (see F13) |\n103|| 15 | `Inspect` failure → precondition | narrowed to `/zzz` prefix | killed | partial |\n104|| 15b | same, deletion form | fabricate `{IsRegular:true, UID:operator}` | **SURVIVED** | (see F13) |\n105|| 16 | regular-file target | gate deleted | killed | full |\n106|| 17 | approved owner, on every source | deleted; narrowed to `source != \"path\"` | killed | full |\n107|| 18 | `ReadFile` failure → precondition | error swallowed, empty content digested | killed | full |\n108|\n109|### `OwnerPolicy`\n110|\n111|| # | Gate | Mutant | Result | Bucket |\n112|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n113|| 19 | operator-UID approval | branch deleted | killed | full |\n114|| 20 | administrator-UID approval | branch deleted; loosened to \"any uid if the set is non-empty\" | killed | full |\n115|| 21 | no superuser exception | `if uid == 0 { return true }` | killed | full |\n116|| 22 | `OwnerIdentity` carries the uid | returns constant `\"uid:approved\"` | killed | full |\n117|\n118|### `Trust`\n119|\n120|| # | Gate | Mutant | Result | Bucket |\n121|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n122|| 23 | builtin refusal | gate deleted | killed | full |\n123|| 24 | records approving owner | `owner: \"\"` | killed | full |\n124|| 25 | records undisguised source path | `sourcePath: candidate.canon` | killed | full |\n125|| 26 | records trust instant | `trustedAt: scalar.Timestamp{}` | killed | full |\n126|\n127|### `Verify`\n128|\n129|| # | Gate | Mutant | Result | Bucket |\n130|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n131|| 27 | re-resolve failure → `integrity_failure` | narrowed to `/zzz`; deleted | killed | full |\n132|| 28 | canonical-target retarget | gate deleted | killed | full |\n133|| 29 | re-inspect failure → integrity | narrowed to `/zzz` | killed | partial |\n134|| 29b | same, deletion form | fabricate `{IsRegular:true, UID:operator}` | **SURVIVED** | (see F13) |\n135|| 30 | regular-file → integrity | gate deleted | killed | full |\n136|| 31 | owner-**approval** half of the owner gate | `!Approves` clause dropped | killed | full |\n137|| 32 | **recorded**-owner half of the owner gate | `identity != record.owner` clause dropped | killed | full |\n138|| 33 | owner gate holds for a zero-value receipt | skip when `record.owner == \"\"` | **SURVIVED** | **sliver** |\n139|| 34 | re-read failure → integrity | narrowed to `/zzz`; `return nil` | killed | full |\n140|| 35 | digest comparison over all 32 bytes | compare `sum[:1]`; compare `sum[31:]` | killed | full |\n141|| 36 | `digestBytes` length guard | `< size` + zero-fill fallback | survived — **equivalent** (both forms compare unequal) |\n142|| 37 | `digestBytes` non-hex guard | guard removed | survived — **equivalent** (garbage bytes still compare unequal) |\n143|| 38 | `unhex` lowercase-only | uppercase accepted | survived — **equivalent** (`scalar.Digest.Hex()` is lowercase by construction) |\n144|\n145|### `Candidate` absence accessors\n146|\n147|| # | Gate | Mutant | Result | Bucket |\n148|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n149|| 39 | `SourcePath`/`CanonicalPath`/`Digest`/`Owner` report absence for builtins | each `kind != KindExternal` guard neutered | killed (4/4) | full |\n150|\n151|### `OSSystem` — the production filesystem seam\n152|\n153|| # | Gate | Mutant | Result | Bucket |\n154|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n155|| 40 | `ReadDir` error propagation | `return nil, nil` (failure → absence) | **SURVIVED** | **unevidenced** |\n156|| 41 | `Canonicalize` resolves symlinks | `EvalSymlinks` skipped | killed | full |\n157|| 42 | `Canonicalize` `filepath.Abs` error propagation | error swallowed | survived — **equivalent** (`Abs` only fails when `Getwd` does) |\n158|| 43 | `Inspect` stat error propagation | fabricate `{IsRegular:true, UID:geteuid}` | **SURVIVED** | **unevidenced** |\n159|| 44 | `Inspect` owner-attestation error propagation | `uid = 0` on attestation failure | **SURVIVED** | **unevidenced** |\n160|| 45 | `Inspect` stats target, not link | `os.Stat` → `os.Lstat` | survived — **equivalent** (input is already canonical) |\n161|| 46 | `PathDirs` reads `PATH` | returns nil for a non-empty `PATH` | killed | full |\n162|| 47 | `PathDirs` skips empty entries | empty entries kept | **SURVIVED** | **unevidenced** |\n163|| 48 | `CurrentOperatorPolicy` seeds no administrator | seeds `AdministratorUIDs: {0}` | **SURVIVED** | **unevidenced** |\n164|| 49 | `CurrentOperatorPolicy` uses effective uid | `Geteuid` → `Getuid` | **SURVIVED** | **unevidenced** |\n165|| 50 | `fileOwnerUID` (unix) refuses on unavailable metadata | returns `0, nil` | **SURVIVED** | **unevidenced** |\n166|| 51 | `fileOwnerUID` (windows) refuses | returns `0, nil` | **SURVIVED** | **unevidenced (build-tag bound)** |\n167|\n168|### Meta-gates — the derived inventories\n169|\n170|| # | Gate | Mutant | Result | Bucket |\n171|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n172|| 52 | closed refusal-code set | production emits a fourth code `not_supported` | killed | full |\n173|| 53 | `Discover` source-inventory bijection | A1–A5 above | killed (5/5) | full |\n174|| 54 | \"no `os/exec` import\" scan | scan finds no files | killed — floor present (`the check is blind`) | full |\n175|| 55 | \"no capability member\" scan | derives an empty member map | killed — floor present (`the scan is blind`) | full |\n176|| 56 | \"no SDK-advertising exported symbol\" scan | derives an empty symbol list | **SURVIVED** — no floor | **sliver** |\n177|| 57 | refusal inventory: every site exercised | new unexercised production refusal site | killed | partial |\n178|| 58 | refusal inventory: no stray `Error` literal | `Error{...}` minted outside the constructors | killed | partial |\n179|| 59 | refusal inventory: no raw `fmt.Errorf` / `panic` | both minted in `provider.go` | killed | partial |\n180|| 60 | refusal inventory **domain floor** | B1 empty domain / B2 1-of-N domain / H4 skip `provider.go` / B5 wrong-cwd read + planted stray | **SURVIVED (4/4)** | **unevidenced** |\n181|\n182|## 4. Measured ratio\n183|\n184|**59 of 84 mutants killed. 25 survived; 5 of those are behaviourally\n185|equivalent (rows 36, 37, 38, 42, 45), leaving 20 substantive survivors across\n186|9 distinct defects.**\n187|\n188|By gate row (54 rows, excluding the 5 equivalent-mutant rows):\n189|\n190|| Bucket | Rows |\n191|| --- | ---: |\n192|| full | 35 |\n193|| partial | 6 |\n194|| sliver | 3 |\n195|| unevidenced | 10 |\n196|\n197|The three deletion-form survivors on precondition gates (14b, 15b, 29b) are\n198|counted inside their `partial` rows, not as separate rows.\n199|\n200|## 5. Findings\n201|\n202|### F11 — the refusal inventory has no floor on its derived domain (blocking)\n203|\n204|`auditRefusalInventory` derives its domain with `os.Getwd()` + `os.ReadDir` +\n205|skip-`_test.go`, then asserts only *\"every derived site was exercised\"*,\n206|*\"no stray literals\"*, *\"no raw constructors\"*. All three are vacuous on an\n207|empty domain, and an empty domain is produced by a **successful** read of the\n208|wrong directory — no error, no signal.\n209|\n210|Four mutants, four survivals, suite green each time:\n211|\n212|- **B1** `deriveRefusalInventory` returns `refusalInventory{}` → green.\n213|- **B2** domain truncated to 1 of N sites → green.\n214|- **H4** the scan skips `provider.go` entirely — every production refusal site\n215|  in the package — → green.\n216|- **B5** a stray `Error{...}` literal planted in `provider.go` **plus** a\n217|  directory read redirected one level up (an empty-but-successful read, exactly\n218|  what a wrong cwd produces) → **green**. The same stray literal alone (B4)\n219|  reddens. The check is real; its domain can be silently emptied out from\n220|  under it.\n221|\n222|This is F9's defect, one level up, wearing a parser — the shape LOGBOOK 0230\n223|names as the round-2 root cause. It is not a design disagreement: **the\n224|producer already established this floor three times in this same package** —\n225|`TestDiscoveryReachesNoProcess` has `if !found { t.Fatal(\"scanned no\n226|production sources; the check is blind\") }`, `TestCandidatesAdvertiseNoCapability`\n227|has `if len(members) == 0 { t.Fatal(\"derived no candidate members; the scan is\n228|blind\") }`, and the source inventory has exact-count assertions. The refusal\n229|inventory, which uses the identical file-scan idiom, has none. Fourth\n230|occurrence of \"closed the guards the review named, did not enumerate the rest.\"\n231|\n232|Fix: give `deriveRefusalInventory` a floor — a minimum production file count\n233|and a minimum site count, asserted against a derived-not-hand-listed lower\n234|bound — and prove it with the B1/H4 mutants. Row 56 (`exportedSymbols`) needs\n235|the same one-line floor.\n236|\n237|### F12 — the production `OSSystem` seam has zero negative tests (blocking)\n238|\n239|Rows 40, 43, 44, 47, 48, 49, 50, 51: eight survivors, one file. `os_test.go`\n240|contains no `chmod`, no unreadable path, no stat failure, no attestation\n241|failure — `grep -n \"chmod\\|0o000\\|permission\\|Inspect\\|fileOwnerUID\\|Geteuid\"\n242|internal/provider/os_test.go` returns one comment line. Every seam-failure\n243|test in the package drives `fakeSystem`; the fake proves `Discover` reacts\n244|correctly to a reported failure, and proves nothing about whether `OSSystem`\n245|reports one.\n246|\n247|Three of these are F6's twin, not new classes:\n248|\n249|- **Row 44**: `OSSystem.Inspect` swallowing a `fileOwnerUID` error and\n250|  reporting `uid = 0` survives. F6 fixed uid-0 admission in `Approves`; the\n251|  attestation side that *produces* the uid was never attacked.\n252|- **Row 50**: `fileOwnerUID` (unix) returning `0, nil` when\n253|  `info.Sys()` is not a `*syscall.Stat_t` survives — against its own doc\n254|  comment, *\"The host refuses trust when attestation is unavailable rather\n255|  than treating an unknown owner as approved.\"* Trivially testable: the\n256|  function takes an `os.FileInfo`; a stub whose `Sys()` returns `nil` reaches\n257|  it in three lines.\n258|- **Row 48**: `CurrentOperatorPolicy` seeding `AdministratorUIDs: {0}` — a\n259|  root wildcard at the policy-construction site — survives, against its doc\n260|  comment *\"with no additional administrator-approved identities.\"*\n261|\n262|Row 40 (`ReadDir` error → `nil, nil`) is the package's headline invariant\n263|inverted at the only place it can actually be violated: *\"a failed or partial\n264|read is reported as a failure, never as an absence\"* (`doc.go`), restated in\n265|`README.md:400`. Row 51 (native Windows refusal) is a **stated bound**, not a\n266|fixable gap on this host: `os_windows.go` is not compiled on darwin, so no\n267|mutant here can reach it. The README states the Windows behaviour as fact;\n268|either add a `GOOS=windows` vet/build-tagged check or mark the claim as\n269|unverified on this platform.\n270|\n271|### F13 — precondition refusals are pinned by code, not by gate (non-blocking, fix with F12)\n272|\n273|Rows 14b, 15b, 29b. `TestDiscoverRefusesPartialReads` and\n274|`TestVerifyTreatsReadFailureAsIntegrityFailure` assert only\n275|`errorCode(err) == codeLocalPrecondition` / `codeIntegrityFailure`. Deleting\n276|the `Canonicalize`-failure or `Inspect`-failure refusal lets control fall\n277|through to the *next* seam, which also fails, with the *same* code — green.\n278|The narrowing forms redden only because `auditRefusalInventory` notices the\n279|site went unexercised, i.e. the meta-gate is carrying the behavioural test.\n280|With F11 unfixed, that carrier can itself be silently emptied.\n281|\n282|Assert the refusal `Detail()` (or the wrapped cause) so each subtest pins the\n283|gate that fired, not merely the class of the code.\n284|\n285|### F14 — `ax-provider-` is not proven to be an anchor (non-blocking)\n286|\n287|Row 11. `strings.CutPrefix` → `strings.Cut` survives:\n288|`TestDiscoverIgnoresNonCandidateEntries` uses `README.md`, `ax-provider`,\n289|`other-tool` — no name that *contains* the prefix without starting with it.\n290|Under the mutant, `vendor-ax-provider-evil` in a `PATH` directory is\n291|discovered as provider `evil`. This contradicts the spec text the package's\n292|own test quotes: *\"External provider executables are named\n293|`ax-provider-<id>`\"* (`TestSection71TrustRulesArePinned`). One added fixture\n294|name closes it.\n295|\n296|### F15 — `Discover` may return a partial candidate set with a refusal (non-blocking)\n297|\n298|Row 8. `return nil, err` → `return out, err` survives: every refusal test\n299|discards the first return with `_, err := Discover(...)`. `doc.go` and\n300|`README.md:400` both promise *\"instead of yielding a partial set\"* — the\n301|\"instead of\" half is an unsupported claim. Assert `got == nil` in at least one\n302|refusal test per source.\n303|\n304|### F16 — forged-receipt coverage is one point wide (non-blocking)\n305|\n306|Row 33. `TestVerifyRefusesForgedReceipts` forges the digest only, with every\n307|other fact genuine. Skipping the owner gate when `record.owner == \"\"` — the\n308|zero value a truncated or half-deserialized persisted receipt carries —\n309|survives. That is *absent evidence treated as satisfied*, in the one function\n310|whose job is refusing forged evidence. Add a zero-value/empty-field receipt to\n311|that test's domain.\n312|\n313|### F17 — `Builtins()` copy claim untested (non-blocking)\n314|\n315|Row 9. Returning `builtinOrder` directly survives, against the doc comment\n316|*\"The result is a copy; the registry cannot be mutated through it.\"* A caller\n317|mutating the result corrupts discovery order process-wide.\n318|\n319|## 6. What this method cannot see\n320|\n321|Stated bounds, not hedges:\n322|\n323|1. **Build-tag-invisible code.** `os_windows.go` is not compiled on darwin.\n324|   Row 51 is unreachable by any mutant here. `GOOS=windows go vet` would at\n325|   least type-check it; behaviour needs a Windows runner.\n326|2. **No production caller exists.** `grep -rn --include='*.go' 'internal/provider'`\n327|   outside the package returns nothing — there is no `ax` binary wiring\n328|   `Discover`/`Trust`/`Verify` yet. \"Production entry point\" here means the\n329|   package's exported API, which the tests do drive (`TestOSSystemEndToEnd`\n330|   runs the real `OSSystem` over a real temp tree). Whether the host calls\n331|   them correctly is a later leaf and is *not* evidenced by this task.\n332|3. **Concurrency.** Everything ran single-threaded; no `-race`, no TOCTOU\n333|   attack between `Canonicalize`, `Inspect`, and `ReadFile`. A file swapped\n334|   between the stat and the read is a real substitution vector this review did\n335|   not probe.\n336|4. **Equivalent mutants are my judgement.** Rows 36, 37, 38, 42, 45 are called\n337|   equivalent on reasoning (`Digest.Hex()` is lowercase; a canonical path has\n338|   no links; `Abs` fails only when `Getwd` does), not proven so.\n339|5. **The spec-quote pins were read, not mutated.** They are quote-anchored\n340|   with `Contains` + section checks and `t.Fatalf` on miss, so they are not\n341|   structurally vacuous — but I did not mutate `specdoc` itself.\n342|6. **The empty CR delta.** I reviewed `d8fc669..44a4699` and the package as it\n343|   stands. If any work was intended for round 3 that never reached a commit,\n344|   this review cannot see it.\n345|\n346|## 7. Routing\n347|\n348|`to-dev`. F11 and F12 are blocking; F13–F17 are cheap and should ride along.\n349|F11 is the fourth recorded instance of the same enumeration failure and should\n350|be landed in `LOGBOOK.md` as such — the reviewer does not modify the tree, so\n351|the producer lands it."}}}
