n, full `go test ./...` exit 0, tracecheck exit 0 unchanged at 17/403.\\n./LOGBOOK.md:65:- BOUND, unchanged and restated: `tracecheck` still reports `acceptance_cases=74` and `clauses_discharged=17/403`. All eight new tests register against the existing `cli-result-machine-reading` acceptance case rather than new ones, so no coverage figure moved; the registration was probed by renaming a declaration and confirming `tracecheck` names the missing declaration ahead of the projection digest.\\n./LOGBOOK.md:79:- BOUND, unchanged and restated: `tracecheck` still reports `acceptance_cases=74` and `clauses_discharged=17/403`. All three new tests register against existing acceptance cases rather than new ones, so no coverage figure moved; each registration was probed by renaming its declaration and confirming `tracecheck` names the missing declaration ahead of the projection digest.\\n./LOGBOOK.md:93:- BOUND, unchanged and restated: `tracecheck` still reports `acceptance_cases=74` and `clauses_discharged=17/403`. Both new tests register against existing acceptance cases rather than new ones, so no coverage figure moved; the two registrations were probed by renaming each declaration and confirming `tracecheck` names the missing declaration ahead of the projection digest.\\n./LOGBOOK.md:100:- ROOT CAUSE: `README.md` published \\\"73 executable acceptance cases\\\" while `ownership.v0.5.0.json` held 74 entries with 74 distinct ids and `tracecheck` printed `acceptance_cases=74`. The first pass of this leaf moved the registry from 65 to 73 and updated the sentence; the round-2 rework added a case and did not. Nothing measured the figure — setting it to 999 left `go test ./...` and `tracecheck` both at exit 0.\\n./LOGBOOK.md:123:- EVIDENCE: the new test is registered in the `cli-result-machine-reading` acceptance case and the ownership projection digest re-pinned. That registration is not decorative and was not assumed to be checked: renaming the declaration to one that does not exist makes `tracecheck` fail with `declaration ... is absent from \\\"internal/cliresult/client_test.go\\\"` — the declaration-resolution check answers before the digest check does.\\n./LOGBOOK.md:124:- EVIDENCE: `go build`, `go vet`, `gofmt -l ./internal` clean; `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 across 13 packages; `-cover` exit 0 with `cliresult` 95.5% and `axerror` 99.5% (both unchanged — the sweeps add rows through statements already executed); `tracecheck` exit 0 at `acceptance_cases` 74 and `clauses_discharged` 17/403, both unchanged, because a test added to an existing acceptance case discharges no new clause.\\n./LOGBOOK.md:143:- EVIDENCE: 23 mutants, each verified applied, compiled, and carrying the MUTATED text on disk before measurement; 22 killed, 1 declared subsumed, 0 unexplained survivors. Nine narrow rather than delete. `go build`, `go vet`, `gofmt -l` clean; `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 across 13 packages; `-cover` exit 0 with `cliresult` 95.5% and `axerror` 99.5%; `tracecheck` exit 0 at `acceptance_cases` 73 → 74 and `clauses_discharged` 17/403 unchanged — the new acceptance case is attached to the §15.1 and §17.2 bindings as evidence and claims no additional clause, because the gate discharges no obligation the clause scanner measures.\\n./LOGBOOK.md:187:- ROOT CAUSE: **a clause was claimed against a topically related section instead of against the actor its MUST binds.** Ownership clause `15.1#6` at SPEC.md:11047 was discharged by `LocalFromUntrusted`. That line's only RFC 2119 sentence is \\\"The plugin MUST NOT masquerade a different-major object as v2\\\" - it binds the **provider plugin**, a child process this repository does not build; its only binaries are `cataloggen` and `tracecheck`. The host half of the same table row, which `LocalFromUntrusted` does implement, carries no RFC 2119 keyword at all, so it is not what the clause scanner measured.\\n./LOGBOOK.md:192:- EVIDENCE: 26 mutants, each verified applied before measurement, 26 killed, 0 survivors, final restore re-verified uncached. `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 across 12 packages; `go build`, `go vet`, `gofmt -l` clean; `tracecheck` exit 0 at 9/394.\\n===\\nname: CI\\n\\non:\\n  pull_request:\\n  push:\\n    branches:\\n      - main\\n\\npermissions:\\n  contents: read\\n\\njobs:\\n  verify:\\n    name: Verify implementation ownership\\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\\n    timeout-minutes: 10\\n    steps:\\n      - name: Check out repository\\n        uses: actions/checkout@v7\\n\\n      - name: Set up Go\\n        uses: actions/setup-go@v7\\n        with:\\n          go-version-file: go.mod\\n\\n      - name: Verify specification-to-code ownership\\n        run: go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck\\n\\n      - name: Verify generated catalog is current\\n        run: |\\n          go generate ./internal/catalog\\n          git diff --exit-code -- internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go\\n\\n      - name: Test\\n        run: go test ./... -v\\n\\n      - name: Vet\\n        run: go vet ./...\\n\\n      - name: Build\\n        run: go build ./...\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 5460,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1365,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
