{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c6f1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06ed9-7c63-74b3-b8db-139ac4482e30"},"sequence":467,"recorded_at":1780531400000929,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"680c30af-893a-4c96-ab8b-878d612e53c6","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"680c30af-893a-4c96-ab8b-878d612e53c6","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"680c30af-893a-4c96-ab8b-878d612e53c6"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"c9b37d98-3956-4ec6-b9bb-4ca862ead30e"},"task_id":"c9b37d98-3956-4ec6-b9bb-4ca862ead30e","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"c9b37d98-3956-4ec6-b9bb-4ca862ead30e","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.md`.\n(2653 line(s) above)\n2654|### 7.2 Framing and lifecycle\n2655|\n2656|The provider protocol is line-delimited JSON over stdin/stdout with\n2657|<code>protocol = \"urn:ax:protocol:provider\"</code> and\n2658|<code>protocol_version = \"2.0.0\"</code>. Each line MUST be one complete UTF-8\n2659|JSON object no larger than 8 MiB. Stdout MUST contain protocol frames only;\n2660|human diagnostics go to stderr.\n2661|\n2662|<code>ax</code> starts one plugin process per operation. Requests are\n2663|single-flight in v2. After one response, <code>ax</code> closes stdin and the\n2664|plugin MUST exit. Exit 0 requires a successful response. A structured error\n2665|response SHOULD exit 0 because the protocol succeeded; a crash, invalid frame,\n2666|or missing response is a provider-host failure.\n2667|\n2668|Request envelope:\n2669|\n2670|~~~json\n2671|{\n2672|  \"protocol\": \"urn:ax:protocol:provider\",\n2673|  \"protocol_version\": \"2.0.0\",\n2674|  \"request_id\": \"0198f4c8-8e50-7f66-8f70-1234567890ab\",\n2675|  \"operation\": \"doctor\",\n2676|  \"deadline\": \"2026-08-19T04:05:00.000Z\",\n2677|  \"body\": {\n2678|    \"platform\": \"macos\",\n2679|    \"architecture\": \"arm64\",\n2680|    \"provider_executable\": \"/opt/local/bin/pi\",\n2681|    \"identity\": null\n2682|  }\n2683|}\n2684|~~~\n2685|\n2686|The request envelope contains exactly <code>protocol</code>,\n2687|<code>protocol_version</code>, <code>request_id</code> UUIDv7,\n2688|<code>operation</code> from the Section 7.5 operation registry,\n2689|<code>deadline</code> timestamp, and the operation-specific <code>body</code>.\n2690|The deadline MUST be in the future when the host writes the frame.\n2691|\n2692|Success envelope:\n2693|\n2694|~~~json\n2695|{\n2696|  \"protocol\": \"urn:ax:protocol:provider\",\n2697|  \"protocol_version\": \"2.0.0\",\n2698|  \"request_id\": \"0198f4c8-8e50-7f66-8f70-1234567890ab\",\n2699|  \"ok\": true,\n2700|  \"body\": {\n2701|    \"provider_id\": \"pi\",\n2702|    \"provider_version\": \"0.73.1\",\n2703|    \"findings\": []\n2704|  }\n2705|}\n2706|~~~\n2707|\n2708|A success envelope contains exactly <code>protocol</code>,\n2709|<code>protocol_version</code>, <code>request_id</code>, <code>ok = true</code>,\n2710|and the operation-specific <code>body</code>. A failure envelope contains\n2711|exactly the first four members with <code>ok = false</code> plus\n2712|<code>error</code>, and MUST NOT contain <code>body</code>. Envelope and body\n2713|unknown members are protocol errors under major version 2.\n2714|\n2715|Failure envelope:\n2716|\n2717|~~~json\n2718|{\n2719|  \"protocol\": \"urn:ax:protocol:provider\",\n2720|  \"protocol_version\": \"2.0.0\",\n2721|  \"request_id\": \"0198f4c8-8e50-7f66-8f70-1234567890ab\",\n2722|  \"ok\": false,\n2723|  \"error\": {\n2724|    \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:error\",\n2725|    \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n2726|    \"code\": \"capability_unavailable\",\n2727|    \"message\": \"portable store is not available for this provider build\",\n2728|    \"exit_code\": 6,\n2729|    \"retryable\": false,\n2730|    \"details\": {}\n2731|  }\n2732|}\n2733|~~~\n2734|\n2735|Provider protocol <code>2.x</code> statically binds every failure envelope to\n2736|Structured Error <code>1.0.0</code>. The error schema is not independently\n2737|negotiated on a provider invocation; a provider-protocol minor that needs a\n2738|different error schema must explicitly revise that binding. Section 15.1\n2739|defines supported-major, unsupported-major, and invalid-first-frame behavior.\n2740|\n2741|The host MUST terminate a plugin that exceeds its deadline and report\n2742|<code>provider_timeout</code>. It MUST redact environment and stderr before\n2743|logging.\n2744|\n2745|### 7.3 Provider Manifest\n2746|\n2747|The <code>manifest</code> operation requires an empty body and returns\n2748|<code>urn:ax:schema:provider-manifest</code> version <code>1.0.0</code>:\n2749|\n2750|~~~json\n2751|{\n2752|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:provider-manifest\",\n2753|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n2754|  \"provider_id\": \"pi\",\n2755|  \"display_name\": \"Pi\",\n2756|  \"plugin_version\": \"0.1.0\",\n2757|  \"provider_version_range\": \">=0.73.1 <0.74.0\",\n2758|  \"platforms\": [\"linux\", \"macos\", \"windows\", \"wsl2\"],\n2759|  \"operations\": [\n2760|    \"manifest\",\n2761|    \"probe\",\n2762|    \"launch\",\n2763|    \"identify-session\",\n2764|    \"quiesce\",\n2765|    \"native-store-plan\",\n2766|    \"capture\",\n2767|    \"materialize\",\n2768|    \"materialize-status\",\n2769|    \"materialize-commit\",\n2770|    \"materialize-rollback\",\n2771|    \"resume\",\n2772|    \"fork\",\n2773|    \"stop\",\n2774|    \"doctor\"\n2775|  ],\n2776|  \"capability_names\": [\n2777|    \"native_resume\",\n2778|    \"portable_store\",\n(more lines below)"}}}
