{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c715","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06ed9-7c63-74b3-b8db-139ac4482e30"},"sequence":485,"recorded_at":1780531400000965,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"680c30af-893a-4c96-ab8b-878d612e53c6","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"680c30af-893a-4c96-ab8b-878d612e53c6","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"680c30af-893a-4c96-ab8b-878d612e53c6"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"e08db204-50b4-4c44-a2c3-51b26ef69a2f"},"task_id":"e08db204-50b4-4c44-a2c3-51b26ef69a2f","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"e08db204-50b4-4c44-a2c3-51b26ef69a2f","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.md`.\n(2777 line(s) above)\n2778|    \"portable_store\",\n2779|    \"managed_pty\",\n2780|    \"appserver\",\n2781|    \"task_board_primary\",\n2782|    \"prompt_spawn\",\n2783|    \"native_goal_binding\"\n2784|  ]\n2785|}\n2786|~~~\n2787|\n2788|The manifest is closed and every displayed member is required.\n2789|<code>display_name</code> is 1–128 UTF-8 characters;\n2790|<code>plugin_version</code> is SemVer; <code>provider_version_range</code> is a\n2791|1–256 character provider-adapter constraint; <code>platforms</code> is a sorted,\n2792|unique non-empty subset of the four platform enums; <code>operations</code> is\n2793|the ordered registry shown in Section 7.5 with no duplicates; and\n2794|<code>capability_names</code> is the exact seven-name ordered registry shown.\n2795|The manifest declares possible surfaces, not runtime availability.\n2796|\n2797|### 7.4 Capability result\n2798|\n2799|The <code>probe</code> operation body contains platform, architecture,\n2800|provider executable path, and requested capability names. Its response MUST\n2801|identify the exact provider version and emit every known capability using\n2802|<code>urn:ax:schema:provider-probe</code> version <code>1.0.0</code>:\n2803|\n2804|~~~json\n2805|{\n2806|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:provider-probe\",\n2807|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n2808|  \"provider_id\": \"pi\",\n2809|  \"provider_version\": \"0.73.1\",\n2810|  \"platform\": \"macos\",\n2811|  \"architecture\": \"arm64\",\n2812|  \"capabilities\": {\n2813|    \"native_resume\": {\n2814|      \"status\": \"available\",\n2815|      \"enabled\": true,\n2816|      \"evidence\": \"probed\",\n2817|      \"detail\": \"--session, --continue, and --resume are present\"\n2818|    },\n2819|    \"portable_store\": {\n2820|      \"status\": \"conditional\",\n2821|      \"enabled\": false,\n2822|      \"evidence\": \"acceptance_required\",\n2823|      \"detail\": \"closed-store cross-host fixture has not passed\"\n2824|    },\n2825|    \"managed_pty\": {\n2826|      \"status\": \"conditional\",\n2827|      \"enabled\": false,\n2828|      \"evidence\": \"acceptance_required\",\n2829|      \"detail\": \"platform PTY interruption and flush gate has not passed\"\n2830|    },\n2831|    \"appserver\": {\n2832|      \"status\": \"unsupported\",\n2833|      \"enabled\": false,\n2834|      \"evidence\": \"provider_contract\",\n2835|      \"detail\": \"Pi RPC is not claimed as the ax appserver capability\"\n2836|    },\n2837|    \"task_board_primary\": {\n2838|      \"status\": \"unknown\",\n2839|      \"enabled\": false,\n2840|      \"evidence\": \"none\",\n2841|      \"detail\": \"no reliable primary adapter is accepted\"\n2842|    },\n2843|    \"prompt_spawn\": {\n2844|      \"status\": \"unknown\",\n2845|      \"enabled\": false,\n2846|      \"evidence\": \"none\",\n2847|      \"detail\": \"not claimed for v0.3.0\"\n2848|    },\n2849|    \"native_goal_binding\": {\n2850|      \"status\": \"unsupported\",\n2851|      \"enabled\": false,\n2852|      \"evidence\": \"provider_contract\",\n2853|      \"detail\": \"no native task-board goal binding\"\n2854|    }\n2855|  },\n2856|  \"warnings\": []\n2857|}\n2858|~~~\n2859|\n2860|The probe object is closed and every displayed member is required.\n2861|<code>provider_version</code> is a 1–128 character exact version string,\n2862|architecture is <code>amd64</code> or <code>arm64</code>, and\n2863|<code>capabilities</code> contains exactly the seven requested registry keys.\n2864|Each capability value contains exactly <code>status</code>,\n2865|<code>enabled</code>, <code>evidence</code>, and a 0–2,048 character\n2866|<code>detail</code>. <code>warnings</code> is a sorted, unique array of at most\n2867|1,024 strings of at most 2,048 characters each.\n2868|\n2869|Status is one of <code>available</code>, <code>conditional</code>,\n2870|<code>unsupported</code>, or <code>unknown</code>. Only\n2871|<code>available</code> MAY set <code>enabled</code> true. Evidence is one of\n2872|<code>documented</code>, <code>probed</code>, <code>accepted_test</code>,\n2873|<code>provider_contract</code>, <code>inferred</code>,\n2874|<code>acceptance_required</code>, or <code>none</code>.\n2875|\n2876|### 7.5 Required operations\n2877|\n2878|All plugins MUST implement every operation and return\n2879|<code>capability_unavailable</code> when the provider lacks the surface.\n2880|\n2881|Every request and success <code>body</code> is a closed object. The following\n2882|embedded types are part of provider protocol 2.0.0:\n2883|\n2884|| Type | Exact members and constraints |\n2885|| --- | --- |\n2886|| <code>LeaseToken</code> | <code>session_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>lease_epoch:uint53 &gt; 0</code>, <code>lease_id:UUIDv4</code> |\n2887|| <code>WorkspacePaths</code> | <code>map(UUIDv7,absolute-path)[1..256]</code>; paths are destination-native, canonical, and contain no NUL |\n2888|| <code>TerminalDescriptor</code> | <code>backend:tmux&#124;conpty</code>, <code>terminal_id:string[1..512]</code>, <code>interactive:boolean</code>, <code>columns:uint16[1..1000]</code>, <code>rows:uint16[1..1000]</code> |\n2889|| <code>ProcessObservation</code> | <code>terminal_id:string[1..512]</code>, <code>executable_path:absolute-path</code>, <code>started_at:timestamp</code>, <code>candidate_store_paths:sorted unique absolute-path[0..256]</code>, <code>candidate_native_ids:sorted unique string[0..256]</code>; no PID is carried |\n2890|| <code>SpawnPlan</code> | <code>argv:array&lt;string&gt;[1..128]</code>, <code>cwd:absolute-path</code>, <code>env_names:sorted unique environment-name[0..64]</code>, <code>env_literals:map(environment-name,string)[0..64]</code>, <code>native_session_id:string[1..512]&#124;null</code>, <code>profile_mapping:string[1..512]</code>, <code>extensions:object</code>; argv/literal limits and secret rules equal Section 5.1 |\n2891|| <code>SafeBoundaryProof</code> | <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>provider_version:string[1..128]</code>, <code>input_blocked:boolean</code>, <code>boundary_ref:string[1..1024]&#124;null</code>, <code>foreground_idle:boolean</code>, <code>background_idle:boolean&#124;null</code>, <code>open_child_count:uint53</code>, <code>open_database_handle_count:uint53</code>, <code>store_generation:string[1..512]&#124;null</code>, <code>safe:boolean</code>, <code>blockers:sorted unique enum[0..5]</code> |\n2892|| <code>ValidationEvidence</code> | <code>code:string[1..128]</code>, <code>status:passed&#124;skipped</code>, <code>detail:string[0..2048]</code> |\n2893|| <code>NativeDiscoveryProof</code> | <code>native_session_id:string[1..512]</code>, <code>discovered:boolean</code>, <code>discovery_root:absolute-path&#124;null</code>, <code>backend_resolved:boolean</code> |\n2894|| <code>ProcessClosure</code> | <code>process_closed:boolean</code>, <code>store_closed:boolean</code>, <code>exit_code:int32&#124;null</code>, <code>remaining_process_handles:sorted unique string[0..256]</code>, <code>final_store_generation:string[1..512]&#124;null</code> |\n2895|| <code>DoctorFinding</code> | <code>severity:info&#124;warning&#124;error</code>, <code>code:string[1..128]</code>, <code>message:string[1..4096]</code>, <code>remediation:string[1..4096]&#124;null</code>, <code>evidence:documented&#124;probed&#124;accepted_test&#124;provider_contract&#124;inferred&#124;acceptance_required&#124;none</code> |\n2896|| <code>ProviderStoreAuthority</code> | <code>authority_id:root-id</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>platform:macos&#124;linux&#124;wsl2&#124;windows</code>, <code>root_path:absolute-path</code>, <code>root_role:durable_store&#124;durable_index&#124;derived_cache</code>, <code>access:capture_source&#124;materialize_destination</code> |\n2897|| <code>AuthorityTarget</code> | <code>authority_id:root-id</code>, <code>relative_path:.&#124;path</code> |\n2898|| <code>ProviderCaptureItem</code> | <code>source_authority_id:root-id</code>, <code>source_relative_path:path</code>, <code>manifest_path:path</code>, <code>kind:file&#124;directory</code>, <code>state_class:durable_payload&#124;durable_index&#124;derived_cache</code>, <code>required:boolean</code> |\n2899|| <code>ProviderCapturePlan</code> | <code>capture_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>source_authorities:ProviderStoreAuthority[1..32]</code>, <code>items:ProviderCaptureItem[1..32768]</code>, <code>excluded_targets:AuthorityTarget[0..4096]</code>, <code>store_generation:string[1..512]</code>, <code>snapshot_requires_closed_store:boolean</code> |\n2900|| <code>ObjectSink</code> | <code>root:absolute-path</code>, <code>layout:sha256_loose_v1</code>, <code>create_mode:exclusive</code>, <code>max_bytes:uint53</code>, <code>max_blobs:uint53</code> |\n2901|| <code>ProviderObjectSourceAuthority</code> | <code>authority_id:provider_objects</code>, <code>kind:provider_object_source</code>, <code>root_path:absolute-path</code>, <code>layout:sha256_loose_v1</code>, <code>access:read_only</code>, <code>materialization_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>manifest_ids:sorted unique digest[1..1024]</code>, <code>max_bytes:uint53</code>, <code>max_blobs:uint53</code> |\n2902|| <code>ProviderTransactionAuthority</code> | <code>authority_id:provider_transaction</code>, <code>kind:provider_transaction</code>, <code>root_path:absolute-path</code>, <code>layout:provider_transaction_v1</code>, <code>access:read_write</code>, <code>materialization_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>transaction_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>plan_id:digest</code>, <code>same_filesystem_provider_authority_ids:sorted unique root-id[1..32]</code> |\n2903|| <code>ProviderTransactionEntry</code> | <code>sequence:uint53&gt;0</code>, <code>provider_authority_id:root-id</code>, <code>target_relative_path:path</code>, <code>expected_prior_digest:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>prior_kind:absent&#124;file&#124;directory&#124;symlink&#124;hardlink</code>, <code>backup_relative_path:path&#124;null</code>, <code>applied:boolean</code>, <code>restored:boolean</code> |\n2904|| <code>ProviderTransactionDocument</code> | <code>protocol:urn:ax:protocol:provider</code>, <code>protocol_version:2.0.0</code>, <code>document_kind:materialization_transaction</code>, <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>materialization_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>transaction_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>plan_id:digest</code>, <code>state:preparing&#124;prepared&#124;committing&#124;committed&#124;rolling_back&#124;rolled_back</code>, <code>rollback_token:base64url-256+&#124;null</code>, <code>entries:ProviderTransactionEntry[1..65536]</code>, <code>native_discovery:NativeDiscoveryProof&#124;null</code>, <code>created_at:timestamp</code>, <code>updated_at:timestamp</code>, <code>terminal_at:timestamp&#124;null</code> |\n2905|| <code>ProviderTransactionStatus</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>materialization_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>transaction_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>transaction_authority_id:provider_transaction</code>, <code>plan_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>state:unknown&#124;prepared&#124;committed&#124;rolled_back</code>, <code>rollback_token:base64url-256+&#124;null</code>, <code>native_discovery:NativeDiscoveryProof&#124;null</code> |\n2906|\n2907|The <code>SafeBoundaryProof.blockers</code> enum is\n2908|<code>background_unproven</code>, <code>child_process_open</code>,\n2909|<code>database_handle_open</code>, <code>provider_busy</code>, or\n2910|<code>store_unstable</code>. A safe proof requires empty blockers,\n2911|<code>input_blocked</code>, <code>foreground_idle</code>,\n2912|<code>background_idle = true</code>, both counts zero, and non-null boundary and\n2913|store generation. <code>ValidationEvidence</code> arrays MUST be sorted by\n2914|<code>code</code> with no duplicate code. Opaque process handles are valid only\n2915|for the operation lifetime and MUST NOT be persisted or replicated.\n2916|\n2917|The <code>root-id</code> grammar is\n2918|<code>[a-z][a-z0-9_-]{0,63}</code>. Capture authorities are sorted by\n2919|<code>authority_id</code>, have <code>access = capture_source</code>, and are\n2920|unique. Capture items are sorted by <code>manifest_path</code>; each authority\n2921|reference MUST resolve, and\n2922|<code>root_path/source_relative_path</code> MUST remain under that exact root\n2923|after symlink/reparse-point resolution. Items MUST neither overlap nor traverse\n2924|through a symlink. Excluded targets are sorted by authority ID then relative\n2925|path and MUST reference the same authority set. <code>derived_cache</code> is\n2926|included only when Section 8 identifies it as required discovery metadata;\n2927|otherwise it must be excluded. Provider roots that contain credentials,\n2928|machine authentication, runtime sockets, locks, or live ax state MUST be\n2929|rejected even when a plugin names them. <code>ObjectSink.root</code> is a fresh owner-only directory\n2930|created by <code>ax</code>. Under <code>sha256_loose_v1</code>, a plugin writes\n2931|each complete blob with create-new semantics at\n2932|the exact Section 3.2 <code>digest_path_v1</code> relative path\n2933|<code>sha256/HH/REST</code> (two-hex shard, 62-hex leaf).\n2934|It MUST NOT create symlinks, hardlinks, devices, sockets, or any file not named\n2935|by its returned descriptors. The host independently hashes every sink file,\n2936|checks size/limits/exclusions, and only then imports it into the ax object\n2937|store. A plugin never receives the live object-store root.\n2938|\n2939|The destination host, not the peer and not the plugin, constructs both\n2940|materialization authorities. A <code>ProviderObjectSourceAuthority.root_path</code>\n2941|MUST equal\n2942|<code>&lt;state&gt;/provider-object-sources/&lt;materialization-id&gt;/&lt;provider-id&gt;</code>;\n2943|it is a fresh owner-only directory containing exactly the verified manifest\n2944|closure at the same <code>digest_path_v1</code> paths. The host makes every file read-only\n2945|before invoking the plugin. The authority's manifest IDs, byte/blob limits,\n2946|materialization ID, and provider ID MUST equal the selected checkpoint and\n2947|plan. An extra file, writable file, symlink, digest mismatch, or path supplied\n2948|by a remote request is <code>integrity_failure</code>.\n2949|\n2950|A <code>ProviderTransactionAuthority.root_path</code> MUST equal\n2951|<code>&lt;state&gt;/provider-transactions/&lt;provider-id&gt;/&lt;transaction-id&gt;</code>.\n2952|It is a fresh owner-only directory, is disjoint from the object source and all\n2953|plan roots, and names exactly the materialization/provider/transaction/plan in\n2954|the authority. Its\n2955|<code>same_filesystem_provider_authority_ids</code> MUST equal the sorted set of\n2956|all <code>provider_store</code> RootAuthority IDs used by plan operations. The\n2957|host MUST prove that the transaction root and every named provider-store root\n2958|are on the same filesystem/volume before the first plugin mutation. If one is\n2959|not, provider protocol 2.0.0 fails with <code>atomic_commit_unavailable</code>; it MUST\n2960|NOT fall back to an in-place cross-filesystem copy.\n2961|\n2962|The <code>provider_transaction_v1</code> layout contains only these durable\n2963|paths, plus one same-directory temporary file while atomically replacing\n2964|<code>transaction.json</code>:\n2965|\n2966|~~~text\n2967|transaction.json\n2968|staged/<provider-authority-id>/<operation-sequence>\n2969|backups/<provider-authority-id>/<operation-sequence>\n2970|~~~\n2971|\n2972|<code>transaction.json</code> is the UTF-8 JCS encoding of the closed\n2973|<code>ProviderTransactionDocument</code>. Entries are sorted by sequence and\n2974|are exactly the provider-store operations in the plan. For a pre-existing\n2975|target, <code>backup_relative_path</code> is exactly\n2976|<code>backups/&lt;provider-authority-id&gt;/&lt;operation-sequence&gt;</code>; an absent\n2977|target requires <code>prior_kind = absent</code>, a null backup path, and a null\n2978|expected prior digest. Every other prior kind requires that exact non-null\n2979|backup path and a non-null expected prior digest. A prepared document has every\n2980|entry applied, no entry restored, a non-null rollback token, and non-null native\n2981|discovery. A committed document keeps the applied facts, sets the token to\n2982|null, removes every staged/backup payload from disk, and has non-null\n2983|discovery. A rolled-\n2984|back document has every pre-existing entry restored, every transaction-created\n2985|target removed, a null token, and discovery describing the restored\n2986|destination. The plugin MUST fsync a staged replacement and the\n2987|transaction document, atomically rename any predecessor into its backup, then\n2988|atomically rename the staged replacement into the exact target. Each document\n2989|transition is written to a fresh temporary regular file, fsynced, renamed over\n2990|<code>transaction.json</code>, and followed by a parent-directory fsync where\n2991|the platform supports it. Windows uses replace/write-through semantics with\n2992|equivalent user-only DACLs.\n2993|\n2994|<code>terminal_at</code> is null in <code>preparing</code>,\n2995|<code>prepared</code>, <code>committing</code>, and\n2996|<code>rolling_back</code> states and non-null in\n2997|<code>committed|rolled_back</code> states.\n2998|<code>updated_at</code> never precedes <code>created_at</code>, and terminal time\n2999|never precedes either. Timestamps are diagnostics; state, IDs, entry facts, and\n3000|filesystem verification decide recovery.\n3001|\n3002|Every transaction operation receives the same complete\n3003|<code>ProviderTransactionAuthority</code>. A fresh plugin process locates state\n3004|only through that authority, validates the path and\n3005|<code>transaction.json</code> IDs before acting, and MUST NOT use an ambient\n3006|transaction registry or search another root. A crash while\n3007|<code>preparing</code>, <code>committing</code>, or <code>rolling_back</code> is\n3008|reconciled from the entries to one exposed status before\n3009|<code>materialize-status</code> responds; an irreconcilable entry is\n3010|<code>integrity_failure</code> and retains the root for diagnosis. Prepared\n3011|documents store the rollback token under owner-only permissions so a later\n3012|process can reconstruct the current durable status; terminal documents set it\n3013|to null.\n3014|Commit removes all backups only after durable committed state; rollback\n3015|restores all predecessors before durable rolled-back state. The terminal\n3016|<code>transaction.json</code> receipt remains until the corresponding\n3017|Materialization Journal is terminal and for at least\n3018|<code>sync.staging_retention_hours</code> afterward. Object-source bytes and\n3019|backup/staged subtrees MAY then be removed; live or ambiguous roots MUST NOT be\n3020|garbage-collected.\n3021|\n3022|In <code>ProviderTransactionStatus</code>, <code>unknown</code> requires null\n3023|plan/token/discovery; <code>prepared</code> requires all three non-null;\n3024|<code>committed</code> and <code>rolled_back</code> require a non-null plan and\n3025|discovery proof and a null rollback token. The discovery proof in a rolled-back\n3026|status describes the destination after rollback. An operation failure does not\n3027|invent a status state: it returns the protocol failure envelope, and the next\n(more lines below)"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c717","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06ed9-7c63-74b3-b8db-139ac4482e30"},"sequence":486,"recorded_at":1780531400000967,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"680c30af-893a-4c96-ab8b-878d612e53c6","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"680c30af-893a-4c96-ab8b-878d612e53c6","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"680c30af-893a-4c96-ab8b-878d612e53c6"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"e08db204-50b4-4c44-a2c3-51b26ef69a2f"},"task_id":"e08db204-50b4-4c44-a2c3-51b26ef69a2f","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"e08db204-50b4-4c44-a2c3-51b26ef69a2f"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c719","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06ed9-7c63-74b3-b8db-139ac4482e30"},"sequence":487,"recorded_at":1780531400000969,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"680c30af-893a-4c96-ab8b-878d612e53c6","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"680c30af-893a-4c96-ab8b-878d612e53c6","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"680c30af-893a-4c96-ab8b-878d612e53c6"},"call_id":"call_01a06eda5ede77838f08590f9ad327f2","text":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.md`.\n(2777 line(s) above)\n2778|    \"portable_store\",\n2779|    \"managed_pty\",\n2780|    \"appserver\",\n2781|    \"task_board_primary\",\n2782|    \"prompt_spawn\",\n2783|    \"native_goal_binding\"\n2784|  ]\n2785|}\n2786|~~~\n2787|\n2788|The manifest is closed and every displayed member is required.\n2789|<code>display_name</code> is 1–128 UTF-8 characters;\n2790|<code>plugin_version</code> is SemVer; <code>provider_version_range</code> is a\n2791|1–256 character provider-adapter constraint; <code>platforms</code> is a sorted,\n2792|unique non-empty subset of the four platform enums; <code>operations</code> is\n2793|the ordered registry shown in Section 7.5 with no duplicates; and\n2794|<code>capability_names</code> is the exact seven-name ordered registry shown.\n2795|The manifest declares possible surfaces, not runtime availability.\n2796|\n2797|### 7.4 Capability result\n2798|\n2799|The <code>probe</code> operation body contains platform, architecture,\n2800|provider executable path, and requested capability names. Its response MUST\n2801|identify the exact provider version and emit every known capability using\n2802|<code>urn:ax:schema:provider-probe</code> version <code>1.0.0</code>:\n2803|\n2804|~~~json\n2805|{\n2806|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:provider-probe\",\n2807|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n2808|  \"provider_id\": \"pi\",\n2809|  \"provider_version\": \"0.73.1\",\n2810|  \"platform\": \"macos\",\n2811|  \"architecture\": \"arm64\",\n2812|  \"capabilities\": {\n2813|    \"native_resume\": {\n2814|      \"status\": \"available\",\n2815|      \"enabled\": true,\n2816|      \"evidence\": \"probed\",\n2817|      \"detail\": \"--session, --continue, and --resume are present\"\n2818|    },\n2819|    \"portable_store\": {\n2820|      \"status\": \"conditional\",\n2821|      \"enabled\": false,\n2822|      \"evidence\": \"acceptance_required\",\n2823|      \"detail\": \"closed-store cross-host fixture has not passed\"\n2824|    },\n2825|    \"managed_pty\": {\n2826|      \"status\": \"conditional\",\n2827|      \"enabled\": false,\n2828|      \"evidence\": \"acceptance_required\",\n2829|      \"detail\": \"platform PTY interruption and flush gate has not passed\"\n2830|    },\n2831|    \"appserver\": {\n2832|      \"status\": \"unsupported\",\n2833|      \"enabled\": false,\n2834|      \"evidence\": \"provider_contract\",\n2835|      \"detail\": \"Pi RPC is not claimed as the ax appserver capability\"\n2836|    },\n2837|    \"task_board_primary\": {\n2838|      \"status\": \"unknown\",\n2839|      \"enabled\": false,\n2840|      \"evidence\": \"none\",\n2841|      \"detail\": \"no reliable primary adapter is accepted\"\n2842|    },\n2843|    \"prompt_spawn\": {\n2844|      \"status\": \"unknown\",\n2845|      \"enabled\": false,\n2846|      \"evidence\": \"none\",\n2847|      \"detail\": \"not claimed for v0.3.0\"\n2848|    },\n2849|    \"native_goal_binding\": {\n2850|      \"status\": \"unsupported\",\n2851|      \"enabled\": false,\n2852|      \"evidence\": \"provider_contract\",\n2853|      \"detail\": \"no native task-board goal binding\"\n2854|    }\n2855|  },\n2856|  \"warnings\": []\n2857|}\n2858|~~~\n2859|\n2860|The probe object is closed and every displayed member is required.\n2861|<code>provider_version</code> is a 1–128 character exact version string,\n2862|architecture is <code>amd64</code> or <code>arm64</code>, and\n2863|<code>capabilities</code> contains exactly the seven requested registry keys.\n2864|Each capability value contains exactly <code>status</code>,\n2865|<code>enabled</code>, <code>evidence</code>, and a 0–2,048 character\n2866|<code>detail</code>. <code>warnings</code> is a sorted, unique array of at most\n2867|1,024 strings of at most 2,048 characters each.\n2868|\n2869|Status is one of <code>available</code>, <code>conditional</code>,\n2870|<code>unsupported</code>, or <code>unknown</code>. Only\n2871|<code>available</code> MAY set <code>enabled</code> true. Evidence is one of\n2872|<code>documented</code>, <code>probed</code>, <code>accepted_test</code>,\n2873|<code>provider_contract</code>, <code>inferred</code>,\n2874|<code>acceptance_required</code>, or <code>none</code>.\n2875|\n2876|### 7.5 Required operations\n2877|\n2878|All plugins MUST implement every operation and return\n2879|<code>capability_unavailable</code> when the provider lacks the surface.\n2880|\n2881|Every request and success <code>body</code> is a closed object. The following\n2882|embedded types are part of provider protocol 2.0.0:\n2883|\n2884|| Type | Exact members and constraints |\n2885|| --- | --- |\n2886|| <code>LeaseToken</code> | <code>session_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>lease_epoch:uint53 &gt; 0</code>, <code>lease_id:UUIDv4</code> |\n2887|| <code>WorkspacePaths</code> | <code>map(UUIDv7,absolute-path)[1..256]</code>; paths are destination-native, canonical, and contain no NUL |\n2888|| <code>TerminalDescriptor</code> | <code>backend:tmux&#124;conpty</code>, <code>terminal_id:string[1..512]</code>, <code>interactive:boolean</code>, <code>columns:uint16[1..1000]</code>, <code>rows:uint16[1..1000]</code> |\n2889|| <code>ProcessObservation</code> | <code>terminal_id:string[1..512]</code>, <code>executable_path:absolute-path</code>, <code>started_at:timestamp</code>, <code>candidate_store_paths:sorted unique absolute-path[0..256]</code>, <code>candidate_native_ids:sorted unique string[0..256]</code>; no PID is carried |\n2890|| <code>SpawnPlan</code> | <code>argv:array&lt;string&gt;[1..128]</code>, <code>cwd:absolute-path</code>, <code>env_names:sorted unique environment-name[0..64]</code>, <code>env_literals:map(environment-name,string)[0..64]</code>, <code>native_session_id:string[1..512]&#124;null</code>, <code>profile_mapping:string[1..512]</code>, <code>extensions:object</code>; argv/literal limits and secret rules equal Section 5.1 |\n2891|| <code>SafeBoundaryProof</code> | <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>provider_version:string[1..128]</code>, <code>input_blocked:boolean</code>, <code>boundary_ref:string[1..1024]&#124;null</code>, <code>foreground_idle:boolean</code>, <code>background_idle:boolean&#124;null</code>, <code>open_child_count:uint53</code>, <code>open_database_handle_count:uint53</code>, <code>store_generation:string[1..512]&#124;null</code>, <code>safe:boolean</code>, <code>blockers:sorted unique enum[0..5]</code> |\n2892|| <code>ValidationEvidence</code> | <code>code:string[1..128]</code>, <code>status:passed&#124;skipped</code>, <code>detail:string[0..2048]</code> |\n2893|| <code>NativeDiscoveryProof</code> | <code>native_session_id:string[1..512]</code>, <code>discovered:boolean</code>, <code>discovery_root:absolute-path&#124;null</code>, <code>backend_resolved:boolean</code> |\n2894|| <code>ProcessClosure</code> | <code>process_closed:boolean</code>, <code>store_closed:boolean</code>, <code>exit_code:int32&#124;null</code>, <code>remaining_process_handles:sorted unique string[0..256]</code>, <code>final_store_generation:string[1..512]&#124;null</code> |\n2895|| <code>DoctorFinding</code> | <code>severity:info&#124;warning&#124;error</code>, <code>code:string[1..128]</code>, <code>message:string[1..4096]</code>, <code>remediation:string[1..4096]&#124;null</code>, <code>evidence:documented&#124;probed&#124;accepted_test&#124;provider_contract&#124;inferred&#124;acceptance_required&#124;none</code> |\n2896|| <code>ProviderStoreAuthority</code> | <code>authority_id:root-id</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>platform:macos&#124;linux&#124;wsl2&#124;windows</code>, <code>root_path:absolute-path</code>, <code>root_role:durable_store&#124;durable_index&#124;derived_cache</code>, <code>access:capture_source&#124;materialize_destination</code> |\n2897|| <code>AuthorityTarget</code> | <code>authority_id:root-id</code>, <code>relative_path:.&#124;path</code> |\n2898|| <code>ProviderCaptureItem</code> | <code>source_authority_id:root-id</code>, <code>source_relative_path:path</code>, <code>manifest_path:path</code>, <code>kind:file&#124;directory</code>, <code>state_class:durable_payload&#124;durable_index&#124;derived_cache</code>, <code>required:boolean</code> |\n2899|| <code>ProviderCapturePlan</code> | <code>capture_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>source_authorities:ProviderStoreAuthority[1..32]</code>, <code>items:ProviderCaptureItem[1..32768]</code>, <code>excluded_targets:AuthorityTarget[0..4096]</code>, <code>store_generation:string[1..512]</code>, <code>snapshot_requires_closed_store:boolean</code> |\n2900|| <code>ObjectSink</code> | <code>root:absolute-path</code>, <code>layout:sha256_loose_v1</code>, <code>create_mode:exclusive</code>, <code>max_bytes:uint53</code>, <code>max_blobs:uint53</code> |\n2901|| <code>ProviderObjectSourceAuthority</code> | <code>authority_id:provider_objects</code>, <code>kind:provider_object_source</code>, <code>root_path:absolute-path</code>, <code>layout:sha256_loose_v1</code>, <code>access:read_only</code>, <code>materialization_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>manifest_ids:sorted unique digest[1..1024]</code>, <code>max_bytes:uint53</code>, <code>max_blobs:uint53</code> |\n2902|| <code>ProviderTransactionAuthority</code> | <code>authority_id:provider_transaction</code>, <code>kind:provider_transaction</code>, <code>root_path:absolute-path</code>, <code>layout:provider_transaction_v1</code>, <code>access:read_write</code>, <code>materialization_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>transaction_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>plan_id:digest</code>, <code>same_filesystem_provider_authority_ids:sorted unique root-id[1..32]</code> |\n2903|| <code>ProviderTransactionEntry</code> | <code>sequence:uint53&gt;0</code>, <code>provider_authority_id:root-id</code>, <code>target_relative_path:path</code>, <code>expected_prior_digest:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>prior_kind:absent&#124;file&#124;directory&#124;symlink&#124;hardlink</code>, <code>backup_relative_path:path&#124;null</code>, <code>applied:boolean</code>, <code>restored:boolean</code> |\n2904|| <code>ProviderTransactionDocument</code> | <code>protocol:urn:ax:protocol:provider</code>, <code>protocol_version:2.0.0</code>, <code>document_kind:materialization_transaction</code>, <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>materialization_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>transaction_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>plan_id:digest</code>, <code>state:preparing&#124;prepared&#124;committing&#124;committed&#124;rolling_back&#124;rolled_back</code>, <code>rollback_token:base64url-256+&#124;null</code>, <code>entries:ProviderTransactionEntry[1..65536]</code>, <code>native_discovery:NativeDiscoveryProof&#124;null</code>, <code>created_at:timestamp</code>, <code>updated_at:timestamp</code>, <code>terminal_at:timestamp&#124;null</code> |\n2905|| <code>ProviderTransactionStatus</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>materialization_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>transaction_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>transaction_authority_id:provider_transaction</code>, <code>plan_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>state:unknown&#124;prepared&#124;committed&#124;rolled_back</code>, <code>rollback_token:base64url-256+&#124;null</code>, <code>native_discovery:NativeDiscoveryProof&#124;null</code> |\n2906|\n2907|The <code>SafeBoundaryProof.blockers</code> enum is\n2908|<code>background_unproven</code>, <code>child_process_open</code>,\n2909|<code>database_handle_open</code>, <code>provider_busy</code>, or\n2910|<code>store_unstable</code>. A safe proof requires empty blockers,\n2911|<code>input_blocked</code>, <code>foreground_idle</code>,\n2912|<code>background_idle = true</code>, both counts zero, and non-null boundary and\n2913|store generation. <code>ValidationEvidence</code> arrays MUST be sorted by\n2914|<code>code</code> with no duplicate code. Opaque process handles are valid only\n2915|for the operation lifetime and MUST NOT be persisted or replicated.\n2916|\n2917|The <code>root-id</code> grammar is\n2918|<code>[a-z][a-z0-9_-]{0,63}</code>. Capture authorities are sorted by\n2919|<code>authority_id</code>, have <code>access = capture_source</code>, and are\n2920|unique. Capture items are sorted by <code>manifest_path</code>; each authority\n2921|reference MUST resolve, and\n2922|<code>root_path/source_relative_path</code> MUST remain under that exact root\n2923|after symlink/reparse-point resolution. Items MUST neither overlap nor traverse\n2924|through a symlink. Excluded targets are sorted by authority ID then relative\n2925|path and MUST reference the same authority set. <code>derived_cache</code> is\n2926|included only when Section 8 identifies it as required discovery metadata;\n2927|otherwise it must be excluded. Provider roots that contain credentials,\n2928|machine authentication, runtime sockets, locks, or live ax state MUST be\n2929|rejected even when a plugin names them. <code>ObjectSink.root</code> is a fresh owner-only directory\n2930|created by <code>ax</code>. Under <code>sha256_loose_v1</code>, a plugin writes\n2931|each complete blob with create-new semantics at\n2932|the exact Section 3.2 <code>digest_path_v1</code> relative path\n2933|<code>sha256/HH/REST</code> (two-hex shard, 62-hex leaf).\n2934|It MUST NOT create symlinks, hardlinks, devices, sockets, or any file not named\n2935|by its returned descriptors. The host independently hashes every sink file,\n2936|checks size/limits/exclusions, and only then imports it into the ax object\n2937|store. A plugin never receives the live object-store root.\n2938|\n2939|The destination host, not the peer and not the plugin, constructs both\n2940|materialization authorities. A <code>ProviderObjectSourceAuthority.root_path</code>\n2941|MUST equal\n2942|<code>&lt;state&gt;/provider-object-sources/&lt;materialization-id&gt;/&lt;provider-id&gt;</code>;\n2943|it is a fresh owner-only directory containing exactly the verified manifest\n2944|closure at the same <code>digest_path_v1</code> paths. The host makes every file read-only\n2945|before invoking the plugin. The authority's manifest IDs, byte/blob limits,\n2946|materialization ID, and provider ID MUST equal the selected checkpoint and\n2947|plan. An extra file, writable file, symlink, digest mismatch, or path supplied\n2948|by a remote request is <code>integrity_failure</code>.\n2949|\n2950|A <code>ProviderTransactionAuthority.root_path</code> MUST equal\n2951|<code>&lt;state&gt;/provider-transactions/&lt;provider-id&gt;/&lt;transaction-id&gt;</code>.\n2952|It is a fresh owner-only directory, is disjoint from the object source and all\n2953|plan roots, and names exactly the materialization/provider/transaction/plan in\n2954|the authority. Its\n2955|<code>same_filesystem_provider_authority_ids</code> MUST equal the sorted set of\n2956|all <code>provider_store</code> RootAuthority IDs used by plan operations. The\n2957|host MUST prove that the transaction root and every named provider-store root\n2958|are on the same filesystem/volume before the first plugin mutation. If one is\n2959|not, provider protocol 2.0.0 fails with <code>atomic_commit_unavailable</code>; it MUST\n2960|NOT fall back to an in-place cross-filesystem copy.\n2961|\n2962|The <code>provider_transaction_v1</code> layout contains only these durable\n2963|paths, plus one same-directory temporary file while atomically replacing\n2964|<code>transaction.json</code>:\n2965|\n2966|~~~text\n2967|transaction.json\n2968|staged/<provider-authority-id>/<operation-sequence>\n2969|backups/<provider-authority-id>/<operation-sequence>\n2970|~~~\n2971|\n2972|<code>transaction.json</code> is the UTF-8 JCS encoding of the closed\n2973|<code>ProviderTransactionDocument</code>. Entries are sorted by sequence and\n2974|are exactly the provider-store operations in the plan. For a pre-existing\n2975|target, <code>backup_relative_path</code> is exactly\n2976|<code>backups/&lt;provider-authority-id&gt;/&lt;operation-sequence&gt;</code>; an absent\n2977|target requires <code>prior_kind = absent</code>, a null backup path, and a null\n2978|expected prior digest. Every other prior kind requires that exact non-null\n2979|backup path and a non-null expected prior digest. A prepared document has every\n2980|entry applied, no entry restored, a non-null rollback token, and non-null native\n2981|discovery. A committed document keeps the applied facts, sets the token to\n2982|null, removes every staged/backup payload from disk, and has non-null\n2983|discovery. A rolled-\n2984|back document has every pre-existing entry restored, every transaction-created\n2985|target removed, a null token, and discovery describing the restored\n2986|destination. The plugin MUST fsync a staged replacement and the\n2987|transaction document, atomically rename any predecessor into its backup, then\n2988|atomically rename the staged replacement into the exact target. Each document\n2989|transition is written to a fresh temporary regular file, fsynced, renamed over\n2990|<code>transaction.json</code>, and followed by a parent-directory fsync where\n2991|the platform supports it. Windows uses replace/write-through semantics with\n2992|equivalent user-only DACLs.\n2993|\n2994|<code>terminal_at</code> is null in <code>preparing</code>,\n2995|<code>prepared</code>, <code>committing</code>, and\n2996|<code>rolling_back</code> states and non-null in\n2997|<code>committed|rolled_back</code> states.\n2998|<code>updated_at</code> never precedes <code>created_at</code>, and terminal time\n2999|never precedes either. Timestamps are diagnostics; state, IDs, entry facts, and\n3000|filesystem verification decide recovery.\n3001|\n3002|Every transaction operation receives the same complete\n3003|<code>ProviderTransactionAuthority</code>. A fresh plugin process locates state\n3004|only through that authority, validates the path and\n3005|<code>transaction.json</code> IDs before acting, and MUST NOT use an ambient\n3006|transaction registry or search another root. A crash while\n3007|<code>preparing</code>, <code>committing</code>, or <code>rolling_back</code> is\n3008|reconciled from the entries to one exposed status before\n3009|<code>materialize-status</code> responds; an irreconcilable entry is\n3010|<code>integrity_failure</code> and retains the root for diagnosis. Prepared\n3011|documents store the rollback token under owner-only permissions so a later\n3012|process can reconstruct the current durable status; terminal documents set it\n3013|to null.\n3014|Commit removes all backups only after durable committed state; rollback\n3015|restores all predecessors before durable rolled-back state. The terminal\n3016|<code>transaction.json</code> receipt remains until the corresponding\n3017|Materialization Journal is terminal and for at least\n3018|<code>sync.staging_retention_hours</code> afterward. Object-source bytes and\n3019|backup/staged subtrees MAY then be removed; live or ambiguous roots MUST NOT be\n3020|garbage-collected.\n3021|\n3022|In <code>ProviderTransactionStatus</code>, <code>unknown</code> requires null\n3023|plan/token/discovery; <code>prepared</code> requires all three non-null;\n3024|<code>committed</code> and <code>rolled_back</code> require a non-null plan and\n3025|discovery proof and a null rollback token. The discovery proof in a rolled-back\n3026|status describes the destination after rollback. An operation failure does not\n3027|invent a status state: it returns the protocol failure envelope, and the next\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
