{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c73d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06ed9-7c63-74b3-b8db-139ac4482e30"},"sequence":505,"recorded_at":1780531400001005,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"680c30af-893a-4c96-ab8b-878d612e53c6","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"680c30af-893a-4c96-ab8b-878d612e53c6","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"680c30af-893a-4c96-ab8b-878d612e53c6"},"call_id":"call_01a06eda6c237f61acf6da42bbef8438","text":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.md`.\n(3026 line(s) above)\n3027|invent a status state: it returns the protocol failure envelope, and the next\n3028|status request reports the last durable state. An unreadable or\n3029|integrity-invalid transaction MUST fail with <code>integrity_failure</code> and\n3030|MUST be quarantined rather than represented as a successful status object.\n3031|Every provider mutation request that carries <code>operation_id</code> uses the\n3032|single Provider protocol 2.0.0 idempotency key\n3033|<code>(operation, operation_id)</code>. An\n3034|identical canonical mutation request MUST return a byte-identical result across\n3035|a fresh plugin process; any changed member is\n3036|<code>idempotency_mismatch</code> and MUST cause no new mutation. Observational\n3037|operations, including <code>materialize-status</code>, are evolving reads. They\n3038|use the provider envelope's fresh <code>request_id</code> only for correlation,\n3039|MUST NOT be stored as mutation receipts, and MUST return the durable state at\n3040|the read's reconciliation point even when an earlier identical read returned a\n3041|different phase. For <code>capture</code>, replay verifies/reuses only exact\n3042|digest-named files already present in the same Object Sink and re-emits the\n3043|same manifest/descriptors; an extra or changed file fails integrity. Provider\n3044|<code>fork</code> is side-effect-free and recomputes the same plan. The\n3045|materialize mutations use their durable transaction document as the receipt.\n3046|No operation relies on a searched ambient registry. Transaction IDs and\n3047|mutation operation IDs are caller-supplied and stable across retries. For one\n3048|provider materialization transaction, the <code>operation_id</code> is\n3049|transaction-wide across <code>materialize</code> and exactly one terminal\n3050|<code>materialize-commit</code> or <code>materialize-rollback</code>; a\n3051|<code>materialize-status</code> request omits it and locates the transaction only\n3052|through the caller-supplied materialization/transaction IDs and exact authority.\n3053|Reusing the mutation value across distinct operation tags does not alias their\n3054|recorded results. Within one provider ID,\n3055|an operation ID used by the materialize family identifies exactly one materialization transaction:\n3056|its <code>materialization_id</code>, <code>transaction_id</code>, plan ID, object\n3057|source, transaction authority, provider-store authorities, lease, activation,\n3058|rollback reason, and all remaining body members are immutable retry input for\n3059|their operation tag. Reusing <code>(operation, operation_id)</code> with any\n3060|different canonical body is <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>; the plugin MUST\n3061|return the first recorded result or failure and MUST NOT allocate, search, or\n3062|mutate another transaction root. A transaction or materialization ID already\n3063|bound to another operation ID is also <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>. There\n3064|is no second tuple- or path-based idempotency key in provider protocol 2.0.0.\n3065|\n3066|The operation body registry is exact. A named schema object means the complete\n3067|validated object, not only its digest. Arrays of schema objects are sorted by\n3068|their canonical identity field and contain no duplicate identity:\n3069|\n3070|| Operation | Exact request body | Exact success body |\n3071|| --- | --- | --- |\n3072|| <code>manifest</code> | <code>{}</code> | Provider Manifest object (Section 7.3) |\n3073|| <code>probe</code> | <code>{platform:macos&#124;linux&#124;wsl2&#124;windows, architecture:amd64&#124;arm64, provider_executable:absolute-path&#124;null, requested_capabilities:sorted unique capability-name[0..7]}</code> | Provider Probe object (Section 7.4) |\n3074|| <code>launch</code> | <code>{session_record:Session Record, workspace_paths:WorkspacePaths, execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo, launch_plan:Launch Plan, terminal:TerminalDescriptor}</code> | <code>SpawnPlan</code> |\n3075|| <code>identify-session</code> | <code>{session_id:UUIDv7, provider_id:provider-id, observation:ProcessObservation}</code> | <code>{identity:Provider Identity Record, confidence:exact&#124;strong&#124;weak, matched_evidence:sorted unique native_id&#124;store_path&#124;provider_event&#124;backend_lookup[1..4]}</code> |\n3076|| <code>quiesce</code> | <code>{identity:Provider Identity Record, terminal:TerminalDescriptor, timeout_ms:uint53[1..3600000], lease:LeaseToken}</code> | <code>{proof:SafeBoundaryProof}</code> |\n3077|| <code>native-store-plan</code> | Tagged <code>NativeStorePlanRequest</code>: capture is <code>{phase:capture, identity:Provider Identity Record, source_platform:macos&#124;linux&#124;wsl2&#124;windows, mode:snapshot&#124;handoff&#124;fork, source_workspace_paths:WorkspacePaths, lease:LeaseToken}</code>; materialize is <code>{phase:materialize, identity:Provider Identity Record, source_platform:macos&#124;linux&#124;wsl2&#124;windows, destination_platform:macos&#124;linux&#124;wsl2&#124;windows, destination_host_id:UUIDv7, mode:snapshot&#124;handoff&#124;fork, source_manifest_id:digest, destination_workspace_paths:WorkspacePaths, lease:LeaseToken}</code> | Tagged <code>NativeStorePlanResult</code>: capture is <code>{phase:capture, capture_plan:ProviderCapturePlan, include_classes:sorted unique string[0..128], exclude_classes:sorted unique string[0..128]}</code>; materialize is <code>{phase:materialize, materialization_plan:Materialization Plan, include_classes:sorted unique string[0..128], exclude_classes:sorted unique string[0..128], path_key_rewrites:map(UUIDv7,string[1..1024])[0..256]}</code> |\n3078|| <code>capture</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, capture_plan:ProviderCapturePlan, proof:SafeBoundaryProof, object_sink:ObjectSink, lease:LeaseToken}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, capture_id:UUIDv7, manifest:Transfer Manifest, blob_descriptors:sorted unique Blob Descriptor[0..32768], written_blob_ids:sorted unique digest[0..32768], captured_store_generation:string[1..512], exclusions_applied:sorted unique string[0..128]}</code> |\n3079|| <code>materialize</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, materialization_id:UUIDv7, transaction_id:UUIDv7, plan:Materialization Plan, object_source:ProviderObjectSourceAuthority, transaction:ProviderTransactionAuthority, destination_workspace_paths:WorkspacePaths, lease:LeaseToken}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, materialization_id:UUIDv7, transaction_id:UUIDv7, plan_id:digest, state:prepared, created_paths:sorted unique absolute-path[0..65536], merged_paths:sorted unique absolute-path[0..65536], validations:ValidationEvidence[1..256], rollback_token:base64url-256+, native_discovery:NativeDiscoveryProof}</code> |\n3080|| <code>materialize-status</code> | <code>{materialization_id:UUIDv7, transaction_id:UUIDv7, transaction:ProviderTransactionAuthority}</code> | <code>ProviderTransactionStatus</code> |\n3081|| <code>materialize-commit</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, materialization_id:UUIDv7, transaction_id:UUIDv7, transaction:ProviderTransactionAuthority, rollback_token:base64url-256+, activation:dormant_validated&#124;owner_resumed, lease:LeaseToken}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, materialization_id:UUIDv7, transaction_id:UUIDv7, plan_id:digest, state:committed, backup_removed:boolean, committed_at:timestamp}</code> |\n3082|| <code>materialize-rollback</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, materialization_id:UUIDv7, transaction_id:UUIDv7, transaction:ProviderTransactionAuthority, rollback_token:base64url-256+, reason:lease_lost&#124;validation_failed&#124;resume_failed&#124;operator_abort&#124;crash_recovery}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, materialization_id:UUIDv7, transaction_id:UUIDv7, plan_id:digest, state:rolled_back, restored_paths:sorted unique absolute-path[0..65536], removed_paths:sorted unique absolute-path[0..65536], native_discovery_absent:boolean}</code> |\n3083|| <code>resume</code> | <code>{identity:Provider Identity Record, workspace_paths:WorkspacePaths, execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo, terminal:TerminalDescriptor, lease:LeaseToken}</code> | <code>SpawnPlan</code> |\n3084|| <code>fork</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, source_identity:Provider Identity Record, source_checkpoint:Checkpoint Record, new_session_record:Session Record, destination_workspace_paths:WorkspacePaths, execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo, terminal:TerminalDescriptor}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, result_kind:native_fork&#124;supported_import, planned_native_session_id:string[1..512]&#124;null, spawn_plan:SpawnPlan, requires_provider_materialization:boolean, provenance_verified:boolean}</code> |\n3085|| <code>stop</code> | <code>{identity:Provider Identity Record, terminal:TerminalDescriptor, mode:graceful&#124;force, timeout_ms:uint53[1..3600000], lease:LeaseToken}</code> | <code>{closure:ProcessClosure}</code> |\n3086|| <code>doctor</code> | <code>{platform:macos&#124;linux&#124;wsl2&#124;windows, architecture:amd64&#124;arm64, provider_executable:absolute-path&#124;null, identity:Provider Identity Record&#124;null}</code> | <code>{provider_id:provider-id, provider_version:string[1..128]&#124;null, findings:DoctorFinding[0..1024]}</code> |\n3087|\n3088|For <code>launch</code>, the profile and launch plan MUST exactly equal their\n3089|Session Record values. Provider <code>fork</code> is a planning call: it MUST\n3090|NOT write a provider store, allocate an active backend conversation, or start a\n3091|process. Its operation ID is the Session Record's\n3092|<code>fork_provenance.operation_id</code>; an identical retry returns the same\n3093|plan and any changed body is <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>. The new record\n3094|MUST contain Fork Provenance matching the source/checkpoint and operation, and\n3095|a successful result requires <code>provenance_verified = true</code> and MUST\n3096|NOT describe a blank session. <code>native_fork</code> requires\n3097|<code>requires_provider_materialization = false</code> and MAY have a planned\n3098|native ID when the provider allocates it only at process start.\n3099|<code>supported_import</code> requires\n3100|<code>requires_provider_materialization = true</code>; the coordinator then\n3101|calls <code>native-store-plan phase=materialize</code> with\n3102|<code>mode=fork</code> and includes the validated provider plan in the\n3103|destination materialization transaction. In both variants, a new Provider\n3104|Identity Record is authoritative only after native discovery following the\n3105|prepared transaction; the planned ID is an expectation, not an identity\n3106|record.\n3107|\n3108|<code>launch</code>, <code>resume</code>, and <code>fork</code> return plans; the\n3109|trusted terminal backend performs process creation. Plugins MUST NOT return\n3110|secret environment values. <code>native-store-plan</code> succeeds only for an\n3111|advertised portable-store tuple and MUST separate durable includes,\n3112|machine-local excludes, path-key rewrites, quiescence preconditions, and\n3113|validation steps. Its two request and result variants are closed and disjoint:\n3114|a capture request has no destination platform, destination host, destination\n3115|workspace map, or source manifest; a materialize request has no source\n3116|workspace map. Capture therefore works for the first local checkpoint without\n3117|inventing a destination peer or a source-as-destination sentinel.\n3118|\n3119|The capture result's authorities are the complete provider source-root\n3120|authority for that capture. A materialize plan MUST contain at least one\n3121|Section 10.5 <code>provider_store</code> RootAuthority with\n3122|<code>prepared_for_host_id = destination_host_id</code>. Every such authority\n3123|MUST have the same provider/platform as the request, resolve to a\n3124|destination-local native-store root for the exact adapter tuple, and be\n3125|disjoint from ax data/state/cache/runtime roots, task-board staging,\n3126|workspaces, and credential/authentication roots unless an exact child path is\n3127|the provider's documented durable store. A path-key rewrite is keyed by logical\n3128|workspace ID and contains destination-derived non-secret cache-key data, never\n3129|a source absolute path. An unavailable surface returns the common failure\n3130|envelope, not a success body with a null required plan.\n3131|\n3132|The following source-only first-checkpoint body and result are the normative\n3133|<code>PROVIDER-PLAN-CAPTURE-POS</code> fixture. Their absence of every\n3134|destination member is intentional:\n3135|\n3136|~~~json\n3137|{\n3138|  \"phase\": \"capture\",\n3139|  \"identity\": {\n3140|    \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:provider-identity\",\n3141|    \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n3142|    \"record_id\": \"sha256:3667dd9b0ed92b63daa77d848fa5ad77dd8ca3e5a26a47238133e2094fab8f2d\",\n3143|    \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n3144|    \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n3145|    \"provider_id\": \"codex\",\n3146|    \"provider_version\": \"0.147.0\",\n3147|    \"provider_version_range\": \">=0.147.0 <0.148.0\",\n3148|    \"native_session_id\": \"11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555\",\n3149|    \"identity_kind\": \"session_uuid\",\n3150|    \"logical_workspace_id\": \"0198f4c8-6c30-7d44-8d5e-1234567890ab\",\n3151|    \"backend_realm_fingerprint\": null,\n3152|    \"opaque_identity\": {},\n3153|    \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-4a10-7b22-8b3c-1234567890ab\",\n3154|    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:03:00.000Z\",\n3155|    \"extensions\": {}\n3156|  },\n3157|  \"source_platform\": \"macos\",\n3158|  \"mode\": \"snapshot\",\n3159|  \"source_workspace_paths\": {\n3160|    \"0198f4c8-6c30-7d44-8d5e-1234567890ab\": \"/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/payments-api\"\n3161|  },\n3162|  \"lease\": {\n3163|    \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n3164|    \"lease_epoch\": 1,\n3165|    \"lease_id\": \"aaaaaaaa-bbbb-4ccc-8ddd-eeeeeeeeeeee\"\n3166|  }\n3167|}\n3168|~~~\n3169|\n3170|~~~json\n3171|{\n3172|  \"phase\": \"capture\",\n3173|  \"capture_plan\": {\n3174|    \"capture_id\": \"0198f4c8-0790-72aa-8374-3234567890ab\",\n3175|    \"source_authorities\": [\n3176|      {\n3177|        \"authority_id\": \"codex_sessions\",\n3178|        \"provider_id\": \"codex\",\n3179|        \"platform\": \"macos\",\n3180|        \"root_path\": \"/Users/iv/.codex/sessions\",\n3181|        \"root_role\": \"durable_store\",\n3182|        \"access\": \"capture_source\"\n3183|      }\n3184|    ],\n3185|    \"items\": [\n3186|      {\n3187|        \"source_authority_id\": \"codex_sessions\",\n3188|        \"source_relative_path\": \"2026/08/19/rollout-11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555.jsonl\",\n3189|        \"manifest_path\": \"session/rollout.jsonl\",\n3190|        \"kind\": \"file\",\n3191|        \"state_class\": \"durable_payload\",\n3192|        \"required\": true\n3193|      }\n3194|    ],\n3195|    \"excluded_targets\": [],\n3196|    \"store_generation\": \"closed:11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555:1\",\n3197|    \"snapshot_requires_closed_store\": true\n3198|  },\n3199|  \"include_classes\": [\"durable_payload\"],\n3200|  \"exclude_classes\": [\"credential\",\"live_pid\",\"machine_auth\",\"socket\",\"transient_lock\"]\n3201|}\n3202|~~~\n3203|\n3204|<code>PROVIDER-PLAN-CAPTURE-N1</code> adds\n3205|<code>destination_platform</code> to the capture body and MUST fail with\n3206|<code>incompatible_schema</code>. <code>PROVIDER-PLAN-CAPTURE-N2</code> changes\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
