{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c75d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06ed9-7c63-74b3-b8db-139ac4482e30"},"sequence":521,"recorded_at":1780531400001037,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"680c30af-893a-4c96-ab8b-878d612e53c6","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"680c30af-893a-4c96-ab8b-878d612e53c6","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"680c30af-893a-4c96-ab8b-878d612e53c6"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"1340cb82-18b7-4924-8bfa-2aaf318d93db"},"task_id":"1340cb82-18b7-4924-8bfa-2aaf318d93db","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"1340cb82-18b7-4924-8bfa-2aaf318d93db","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.md`.\n(3205 line(s) above)\n3206|<code>incompatible_schema</code>. <code>PROVIDER-PLAN-CAPTURE-N2</code> changes\n3207|the item authority to an undeclared ID and MUST fail before any provider byte\n3208|is read. <code>PROVIDER-PLAN-CAPTURE-N3</code> makes the source authority equal\n3209|the credential root and MUST fail with <code>secret_policy_violation</code>.\n3210|\n3211|<code>capture</code> is the only provider operation that may emit provider\n3212|payload bytes. It requires <code>proof.safe = true</code>, equal proof/plan store\n3213|generation, and the current lease. Its manifest MUST have\n3214|<code>kind = provider</code>, the session as subject, and exactly the returned\n3215|descriptor/blob closure. The host MUST reject an extra sink file, missing\n3216|required item, descriptor mismatch, excluded class/path, generation change, or\n3217|secret-policy violation and MUST discard the isolated sink without importing\n3218|it. The plugin MUST NOT write a live ax store, live SQLite index, credential\n3219|root, or destination native store during capture.\n3220|\n3221|Provider materialization is a recoverable two-decision transaction.\n3222|<code>materialize</code> applies the exact plan while retaining every replaced\n3223|destination byte under the authorized transaction layout and returns\n3224|<code>state = prepared</code>; it MUST NOT delete its backup. While prepared,\n3225|the host validates exact native discovery and either keeps the replica dormant\n3226|or starts the winning owner. It then calls <code>materialize-commit</code> to\n3227|discard the backup, or <code>materialize-rollback</code> to restore it. Commit\n3228|requires <code>backup_removed = true</code>; rollback requires the native\n3229|identity introduced by the transaction to be absent afterward unless it was a\n3230|pre-existing backend identity. A rollback token is machine-local recovery\n3231|authority, MUST be at least 256 random bits, MUST be stored only in the\n3232|owner-only Materialization Journal and prepared Provider Transaction Document,\n3233|and MUST NOT be replicated or logged.\n3234|\n3235|The provider plugin MUST execute only plan operations whose authority has\n3236|<code>kind = provider_store</code> and whose <code>provider_id</code> equals the\n3237|plugin manifest ID. The ax host executes workspace and task-board operations;\n3238|it MUST reject a plugin response that reports any created or merged path\n3239|outside the selected provider-store authorities. The plugin resolves each\n3240|reported absolute path from that authority's root plus the operation's\n3241|relative target, rechecks the predecessor immediately before mutation, and\n3242|uses no unlisted native-store root. A composite plan is therefore one host\n3243|transaction containing disjoint authority-specific executors, not a grant for\n3244|the provider plugin to mutate the workspace.\n3245|\n3246|The three mutation operations use the same parent <code>operation_id</code>,\n3247|<code>materialization_id</code>, <code>transaction_id</code>, and byte-identical\n3248|transaction authority. The sole mutation idempotency key remains\n3249|<code>(operation, operation_id)</code>; the materialization and transaction IDs\n3250|are immutable non-key inputs. Each mutation tag therefore has a distinct key\n3251|while all phases locate the same authority. A retry of one mutation name MUST\n3252|use byte-identical canonical arguments. <code>materialize-status</code> omits\n3253|<code>operation_id</code>; it is the required evolving lost-response recovery\n3254|read and uses the envelope <code>request_id</code> only for correlation. A status\n3255|read MUST reconcile and return the current durable state, so a read that once\n3256|returned <code>prepared</code> may later return <code>committed</code> or\n3257|<code>rolled_back</code>. An unknown transaction MUST return state\n3258|<code>unknown</code>; the host MUST NOT infer success. A prepared transaction\n3259|survives plugin/host restart until explicit commit or rollback. A plugin that\n3260|cannot provide this prepare/status/commit/rollback behavior MUST advertise\n3261|<code>portable_store</code> disabled.\n3262|\n3263|Normative prepared result body:\n3264|\n3265|~~~json\n3266|{\n3267|  \"operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-e4b0-75cc-9576-1234567890ab\",\n3268|  \"materialization_id\": \"0198f4c8-c290-73aa-9374-1234567890ab\",\n3269|  \"transaction_id\": \"0198f4c8-f5c0-76dd-9677-1234567890ab\",\n3270|  \"plan_id\": \"sha256:64644a5ad573d36c0c13f44f56ef25ab93cff33001ff2a3371b082603910f2dd\",\n3271|  \"state\": \"prepared\",\n3272|  \"created_paths\": [\"/srv/provider/sessions/11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555\"],\n3273|  \"merged_paths\": [],\n3274|  \"validations\": [\n3275|    {\"code\":\"native_discovery\",\"status\":\"passed\",\"detail\":\"exact session identity resolved\"}\n3276|  ],\n3277|  \"rollback_token\": \"YWJjZGVmZ2hpamtsbW5vcHFyc3R1dnd4eXowMTIzNDU2Nzg5QUI\",\n3278|  \"native_discovery\": {\n3279|    \"native_session_id\": \"11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555\",\n3280|    \"discovered\": true,\n3281|    \"discovery_root\": \"/srv/provider/sessions\",\n3282|    \"backend_resolved\": false\n3283|  }\n3284|}\n3285|~~~\n3286|\n3287|The normative transaction cases are:\n3288|\n3289|| Fixture | Calls | Required terminal state |\n3290|| --- | --- | --- |\n3291|| <code>PTX-POS-DORMANT</code> | materialize → status prepared → commit with <code>dormant_validated</code> | committed; replica remains unable to run |\n3292|| <code>PTX-POS-OWNER</code> | materialize → exact discovery → owner resume → commit with <code>owner_resumed</code> | committed; backup removed only after resume evidence |\n3293|| <code>PTX-ROLLBACK</code> | materialize → validation failure → rollback | predecessor bytes restored; introduced identity absent |\n3294|| <code>PTX-LOST-PREPARE</code> | materialize response lost → status prepared | same token/plan returned; no second destination mutation |\n3295|| <code>PTX-LOST-COMMIT</code> | commit response lost → status committed | caller records commit; MUST NOT roll back |\n3296|| <code>PTX-STATUS-EVOLVES</code> | status returns prepared → commit succeeds → the same status body is read under a fresh envelope request ID | second read returns committed; no byte-identical replay rule applies to either observation |\n3297|| <code>PTX-UNKNOWN</code> | status unknown after an ambiguous call | fail closed and quarantine transaction root; MUST NOT infer prepare or commit |\n3298|| <code>PTX-CROSS-PROCESS-COMMIT</code> | process P1 prepares and exits → P2 status reads the same authority/document → P3 commits and exits → P4 status reads the terminal receipt | prepared and committed facts, token, plan, and discovery are identical across processes; backup bytes are removed only by P3 |\n3299|| <code>PTX-CROSS-PROCESS-ROLLBACK</code> | process P1 prepares and exits → P2 rolls back with the same authority/token → P3 status reads the terminal receipt | every predecessor is restored, every introduced target is absent, and no process searches outside the passed authority |\n3300|\n3301|Changing a plan, object-source authority, or transaction authority on a repeated\n3302|<code>materialize</code>, changing activation/lease on a repeated commit, or\n3303|changing rollback reason/token on a repeated rollback while reusing the same\n3304|<code>(operation, operation_id)</code> key is the normative negative\n3305|<code>PTX-IDEMPOTENCY-N1</code> fixture and returns\n3306|<code>idempotency_mismatch</code>.\n3307|\n3308|<code>PTX-IDEMPOTENCY-ID-N1</code> loses a prepared response and retries the\n3309|same <code>(materialize, operation_id)</code> while changing only\n3310|<code>materialization_id</code>; <code>PTX-IDEMPOTENCY-ID-N2</code> changes only\n3311|<code>transaction_id</code>; and <code>PTX-IDEMPOTENCY-ID-N3</code> changes only\n3312|one authority root. Each MUST return <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, leave the\n3313|original transaction document/root byte-identical, and create no second root.\n3314|\n3315|<code>PTX-ROLLBACK-LEASE</code>, <code>PTX-ROLLBACK-VALIDATION</code>,\n3316|<code>PTX-ROLLBACK-RESUME</code>, <code>PTX-ROLLBACK-OPERATOR</code>, and\n3317|<code>PTX-ROLLBACK-CRASH</code> repeat the rollback path with, respectively,\n3318|<code>lease_lost</code>, <code>validation_failed</code>,\n3319|<code>resume_failed</code>, <code>operator_abort</code>, and\n3320|<code>crash_recovery</code>. Each reason is persisted before restoration and\n3321|replaying the same request returns the same terminal result; changing only the\n3322|reason is <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>.\n3323|\n3324|Normative <code>resume</code> request body and success body:\n3325|\n3326|~~~json\n3327|{\n3328|  \"protocol\": \"urn:ax:protocol:provider\",\n3329|  \"protocol_version\": \"2.0.0\",\n3330|  \"request_id\": \"0198f4c8-e4b0-75cc-9576-1234567890ab\",\n3331|  \"operation\": \"resume\",\n3332|  \"deadline\": \"2026-08-19T04:20:00.000Z\",\n3333|  \"body\": {\n3334|    \"identity\": {\n3335|      \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:provider-identity\",\n3336|      \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n3337|      \"record_id\": \"sha256:3667dd9b0ed92b63daa77d848fa5ad77dd8ca3e5a26a47238133e2094fab8f2d\",\n3338|      \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n3339|      \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n3340|      \"provider_id\": \"codex\",\n3341|      \"provider_version\": \"0.147.0\",\n3342|      \"provider_version_range\": \">=0.147.0 <0.148.0\",\n3343|      \"native_session_id\": \"11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555\",\n3344|      \"identity_kind\": \"session_uuid\",\n3345|      \"logical_workspace_id\": \"0198f4c8-6c30-7d44-8d5e-1234567890ab\",\n3346|      \"backend_realm_fingerprint\": null,\n3347|      \"opaque_identity\": {},\n3348|      \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-4a10-7b22-8b3c-1234567890ab\",\n3349|      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:03:00.000Z\",\n3350|      \"extensions\": {}\n3351|    },\n3352|    \"workspace_paths\": {\n3353|      \"0198f4c8-6c30-7d44-8d5e-1234567890ab\": \"/srv/relux/payments-api\"\n3354|    },\n3355|    \"execution_profile\": \"yolo\",\n3356|    \"terminal\": {\n3357|      \"backend\": \"tmux\",\n3358|      \"terminal_id\": \"ax-payments-api\",\n3359|      \"interactive\": true,\n3360|      \"columns\": 120,\n3361|      \"rows\": 40\n3362|    },\n3363|    \"lease\": {\n3364|      \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n3365|      \"lease_epoch\": 4,\n3366|      \"lease_id\": \"aaaaaaaa-bbbb-4ccc-8ddd-eeeeeeeeeeee\"\n3367|    }\n3368|  }\n3369|}\n3370|~~~\n3371|\n3372|~~~json\n3373|{\n3374|  \"protocol\": \"urn:ax:protocol:provider\",\n3375|  \"protocol_version\": \"2.0.0\",\n3376|  \"request_id\": \"0198f4c8-e4b0-75cc-9576-1234567890ab\",\n3377|  \"ok\": true,\n3378|  \"body\": {\n3379|    \"argv\": [\n3380|      \"codex\",\n3381|      \"--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox\",\n3382|      \"resume\",\n3383|      \"11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555\"\n3384|    ],\n3385|    \"cwd\": \"/srv/relux/payments-api/src\",\n3386|    \"env_names\": [\"OPENAI_API_KEY\"],\n3387|    \"env_literals\": {},\n3388|    \"native_session_id\": \"11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555\",\n3389|    \"profile_mapping\": \"--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox\",\n3390|    \"extensions\": {}\n3391|  }\n3392|}\n3393|~~~\n3394|\n3395|### 7.6 Quiescence proof\n(more lines below)"}}}
