{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c77f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06ed9-7c63-74b3-b8db-139ac4482e30"},"sequence":538,"recorded_at":1780531400001071,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"680c30af-893a-4c96-ab8b-878d612e53c6","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.started","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"680c30af-893a-4c96-ab8b-878d612e53c6","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"680c30af-893a-4c96-ab8b-878d612e53c6"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"58d20dde-e844-4886-b766-fb8fef35b286"},"task_id":"58d20dde-e844-4886-b766-fb8fef35b286","event":{"kind":"started","task_id":"58d20dde-e844-4886-b766-fb8fef35b286","span_id":"d7ed925145ab5615"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c781","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06ed9-7c63-74b3-b8db-139ac4482e30"},"sequence":539,"recorded_at":1780531400001073,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"680c30af-893a-4c96-ab8b-878d612e53c6","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"680c30af-893a-4c96-ab8b-878d612e53c6","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"680c30af-893a-4c96-ab8b-878d612e53c6"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"58d20dde-e844-4886-b766-fb8fef35b286"},"task_id":"58d20dde-e844-4886-b766-fb8fef35b286","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"58d20dde-e844-4886-b766-fb8fef35b286","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.md`.\n(3394 line(s) above)\n3395|### 7.6 Quiescence proof\n3396|\n3397|A successful <code>quiesce</code> response MUST contain:\n3398|\n3399|- provider ID and exact version;\n3400|- <code>input_blocked = true</code>;\n3401|- a provider-specific terminal/idle event reference;\n3402|- <code>foreground_idle = true</code>;\n3403|- <code>background_idle = true</code> when the provider can prove it;\n3404|- open child process and open durable-database handle counts, both zero;\n3405|- the last stable provider-store digest or metadata generation; and\n3406|- <code>safe = true</code>.\n3407|\n3408|If background idleness, process exit, or store closure cannot be proven,\n3409|<code>safe</code> MUST be false and graceful takeover MUST stop. A force\n3410|takeover is a separate operator action; the plugin MUST NOT silently convert the\n3411|request.\n3412|\n3413|For a safe direct-provider proof, Checkpoint Safe Boundary Evidence copies\n3414|provider ID/version, input/idle booleans, and maps\n3415|<code>open_child_count</code> to <code>open_processes</code> and\n3416|<code>open_database_handle_count</code> to\n3417|<code>open_database_handles</code>; <code>evidence</code> is the accepted\n3418|adapter mechanism (<code>provider_api</code>, <code>provider_event</code>,\n3419|<code>managed_pty</code>, or <code>accepted_test</code>). RPC\n3420|<code>SafeBoundary</code> additionally copies the boundary reference and store\n3421|generation, sets <code>store_stable = true</code>, and normalizes\n3422|<code>child_process_open</code> to <code>process_open</code>. No other lossy or\n3423|provider-defined mapping is permitted.\n3424|\n3425|### 7.7 Profile mapping\n3426|\n3427|The v0.3.0 <code>yolo</code> mappings are:\n3428|\n3429|| Provider | Required adapter mapping |\n3430|| --- | --- |\n3431|| Codex | <code>--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox</code> (alias <code>--yolo</code> is accepted by current CLI but the long form SHOULD be persisted in diagnostics) |\n3432|| Claude | <code>--dangerously-skip-permissions</code> |\n3433|| Gemini CLI | <code>--approval-mode=yolo</code> |\n3434|| Muse | <code>--yolo</code> |\n3435|| Antigravity | <code>--dangerously-skip-permissions</code> |\n3436|| Pi 0.73.1 | No invented flag; use the provider's default full built-in tool set and report <code>profile_mapping = \"default_unrestricted_tool_set\"</code> |\n3437|\n3438|<code>standard</code> MUST use the provider's normal approval/sandbox behavior\n3439|and MUST omit every unrestricted flag above. It MUST NOT reuse a machine-local\n3440|alias that silently expands to unrestricted mode. Provider-specific standard\n3441|options in a sanitized launch plan are applied only after an exact-version\n3442|probe accepts them.\n3443|\n3444|For Pi 0.73.1, both profiles resolve to the provider's same default full tool\n3445|set because no provider permission-mode flag exists. Probe and launch output\n3446|MUST disclose that equivalence; <code>ax</code> ownership, mesh, conflict, and\n3447|confirmation controls still apply.\n3448|\n3449|The adapter MUST probe the exact provider version before applying a mapping.\n3450|An absent or changed flag fails closed.\n3451|\n3452|### 7.A Provider Protocol 3.0.0 Terminal Instance binding\n3453|\n3454|Provider Protocol 3.0.0 retains the exact v2 framing, request/result envelopes,\n3455|operation registry, idempotency rules, Provider authority, and embedded types,\n3456|except that every occurrence of the v2 <code>TerminalDescriptor</code> is\n3457|replaced by the following closed v3 object:\n3458|\n3459|| Member | Exact type and constraint |\n3460|| --- | --- |\n3461|| <code>terminal_binding_id</code> | digest of the validated Terminal Instance Binding 1.0.0 |\n3462|| <code>terminal_instance_id</code> | AX-assigned UUIDv7; never a PID, socket, path, pipe, URL, handle, token, or native reference |\n3463|| <code>terminal_backend_id</code> | Section 4.B registered backend ID |\n3464|| <code>implementation_version</code> | Semantic Version equal to the admitted Manifest and Probe |\n3465|| <code>protocol_version</code> | Semantic Version in Terminal Backend Protocol major 1 |\n3466|| <code>backend_generation</code> | string[1..256] equal to the host-local binding generation; lengths 0 and 257 are invalid |\n3467|| <code>interactive</code> | boolean |\n3468|| <code>columns</code> / <code>rows</code> | uint16[1..1000] |\n3469|\n3470|No other member is permitted. The descriptor is AX-supplied delegated process-\n3471|hosting context; it conveys no Session ownership, lease, provider identity,\n3472|workspace, checkpoint, replication, or takeover authority to the Provider or\n3473|TerminalBackend. The Provider MUST reject a descriptor whose binding digest,\n3474|backend ID/version, or generation does not match the AX-validated host-local\n3475|binding before launching or observing a provider process. The provider still\n3476|receives the LeaseToken separately and MUST apply its v2 fencing rules.\n3477|\n3478|Provider Protocol 3.0.0 binds Structured Error 1.3.0. A syntactically valid v3\n3479|request receives the v3 envelope with Error 1.3 on failure. A v2/v3 major\n3480|mismatch, an unparseable or oversize first frame, or output that cannot be\n3481|framed follows the Section 15.1 close/termination rule; the caller never trusts\n3482|a different major's error. A dual-stack adapter advertises and validates v2 and\n3483|v3 independently. It MAY translate only <code>ax.tmux</code> and\n3484|<code>ax.conpty</code> to the immutable v2 descriptor under Section 4.E; every\n3485|other backend is <code>incompatible_protocol</code>, not a fallback.\n3486|\n3487|### 7.8 Companion Session Adapter protocol\n3488|\n3489|Cross-environment cloning uses <code>urn:ax:protocol:session-adapter</code>\n3490|1.0.0 in the same trusted <code>ax-provider-&lt;id&gt;</code> executable and with\n3491|the same host-observed executable digest as Provider Protocol 2.0.0. It is not\n3492|a separately discovered plugin. The Session Adapter owns native\n3493|discovery/capture, canonical normalization, isolated projection, and\n3494|independent read-back. Provider 2 and the AX materializer exclusively own\n3495|live-store mutation, rollback custody, publication, and finalization.\n3496|\n3497|The request envelope contains exactly <code>protocol</code>,\n3498|<code>protocol_version</code>, <code>request_id</code>, <code>operation</code>,\n3499|<code>deadline</code>, and <code>body</code>. Success contains the first four\n(more lines below)"}}}
