rtable_store</code> remains C until cross-host fixtures pass. | Authentication files, config secrets, MCP tokens, logs not required by the session, live processes, locks, SQLite/WAL/SHM, and runtime sockets. |\n3866|| Claude | Session UUID; known root <code>~/.claude/projects</code> with a provider-computed project key. | <code>claude --resume SESSION_ID</code>, <code>--continue</code>, and <code>--fork-session</code> when resuming. | Adapter MUST derive the destination project key from the logical workspace mapping, stage the closed session plus documented companion data, and validate explicit UUID resume. It MUST NOT copy the source project-directory key verbatim as identity. <code>portable_store</code> remains C. | OAuth/API credentials, settings secrets, MCP auth, live PTY state, PID/lock/socket files, caches, and unproven companion databases. |\n3867|| Gemini CLI | Session UUID scoped by logical project; documented root <code>~/.gemini/tmp/&lt;project-hash&gt;/chats</code>. | <code>gemini --resume UUID</code>, picker/index/latest, and <code>--session-file FILE</code>. | Adapter MUST compute the destination project hash, prefer the documented session-file import when compatible, stage atomically, then validate <code>--list-sessions</code> and explicit UUID resume. <code>portable_store</code> is C until schema/version and cross-platform fixtures pass. | Google credentials, API keys, settings secrets, trust state, runtime locks, cache-only files, and source path keys. |\n3868|| Muse | Session UUID; <code>$XDG_DATA_HOME/muse/sessions/YYYY/MM/DD/UUID</code>, defaulting below <code>~/.local/share</code>. | <code>muse resume UUID</code>, <code>--last</code>, picker, and <code>muse exec --session-id UUID</code>. Export exists; native import does not. | On probed macOS 0.1.0, a guarded adapter MAY stage the complete closed durable directory, omit transient files, validate with offline export, and resume explicitly. It MUST advertise <code>portable_store = false</code> because cron-aware, current-version, cross-host fidelity is not proven. | <code>~/.config/muse/auth.json</code>, keys, login state, <code>.session.lock</code>, sockets/tokens, live WAL/SHM/locks, updater/plugin caches. <code>cron.db</code> is durable but not safely portable; a session with active or non-empty scheduled work MUST fail materialization. |\n3869|| Antigravity CLI | Conversation UUID plus a destination-authenticated backend/account realm. <code>last_conversations.json</code> maps absolute workspace paths only as local selectors. | <code>agy --conversation UUID</code>, <code>agy -c</code>, and TUI <code>/resume</code>. Desktop-to-CLI picker import is not arbitrary file import. | Materialize the workspace, invoke explicit UUID resume, and allow the provider to rebuild derived cache. A version-aware cache merge MAY map the destination path to UUID. It MUST NOT claim that cache, brain transcript, or SQLite copying recreates a backend-missing conversation. <code>portable_store = false</code>. | OS keyring/account profiles, OAuth/API/MCP secrets, updater locks, live DB/WAL/SHM, sockets, PIDs. Backend resolution is required and a missing UUID MUST fail rather than create a blank replacement. |\n3870|| Pi | Session UUID/file; <code>~/.pi/agent/sessions</code> or the configured <code>PI_CODING_AGENT_SESSION_DIR</code>/<code>--session-dir</code>. | <code>--session PATH_OR_ID</code>, <code>--continue</code>, <code>--resume</code>, <code>--fork</code>. | Adapter MUST snapshot a closed JSONL session and required non-secret companion data, map the destination cwd/session directory, validate the session ID, and resume explicitly. <code>portable_store</code> remains C until versioned cross-host fixtures pass. | <code>auth.json</code>, provider keys/tokens, extension secrets, live process state, locks, sockets, and caches. Pi 0.73.1 has no YOLO flag. |\n3871|| Qwen through task-board | The task-board bundle and manager-owned provider identity; there is no v0.2.1 direct claim and no v0.3.0 direct <code>ax-provider-qwen</code> claim. | Official task-board open/adopt only. | U for direct native materialization. A task-board prompt-mode bundle follows Section 9 and remains opaque. | All private manager/provider state except bytes included by the official bundle exporter. |\n3872|| Future plugin | Declared by plugin and exact probe. | Declared by plugin. | Every cell starts ?/disabled. Promotion requires Section 19 acceptance evidence. | Common exclusions plus plugin-specific exclusions. |\n3873|\n3874|Muse and Antigravity rows above are normative uses of the accepted\n3875|<code>TASK-260819-1ecd6x</code> evidence. The controlled Muse placement probe\n3876|does not create a supported import contract. Antigravity backend resolution is\n3877|native resume but not portable storage.\n3878|\n3879|### 8.3 Capability matrix\n3880|\n3881|| Provider | <code>native_resume</code> | <code>portable_store</code> | <code>managed_pty</code> | <code>appserver</code> | <code>task_board_primary</code> | <code>prompt_spawn</code> | <code>native_goal_binding</code> |\n3882|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n3883|| Codex | A | C | C | A through task-board | A through task-board | A through task-board | A through task-board |\n3884|| Claude | A | C | C | U for direct adapter | A through task-board | A through task-board | A through task-board |\n3885|| Gemini CLI | A | C | C | ? | U | A through task-board | U |\n3886|| Muse | C by platform/version | U | C | ? | U | A through task-board | U |\n3887|| Antigravity CLI | C: backend realm required | U | C | ? | U | ? | U |\n3888|| Pi | A | C | C | U; Pi RPC is not claimed as this capability | ? | ? | U |\n3889|| Qwen through task-board | U direct | U direct | U direct | U direct | U | A through task-board | U |\n3890|| Future plugin | ? | ? | ? | ? | ? | ? | ? |\n3891|\n3892|For Codex and Claude, task-board owns app-server/thread or PTY mechanics,\n3893|reattach, resume, and goal binding. The direct Claude adapter therefore does\n3894|not advertise <code>appserver</code>. The task-board capability plane and\n3895|direct-provider capability plane MUST NOT be conflated.\n3896|\n3897|### 8.4 Provider/platform matrix\n3898|\n3899|Each cell is <code>native resume / cross-host materialization / managed\n3900|terminal</code>. Task-board-only behavior is stated separately.\n3901|\n3902|| Provider/platform | Status | Normative limit |\n3903|| --- | --- | --- |\n3904|| Codex / macOS | A / C / C | Resume and unrestricted flag are documented; portable store and PTY flush require adapter fixtures. |\n3905|| Codex / Linux | A / C / C | Same; exact distribution and filesystem fixture required. |\n3906|| Codex / WSL2 | A / C / C | Treat as Linux with a Linux store. Repositories SHOULD live below the WSL home, not a Windows-mounted path. |\n3907|| Codex / native Windows | A / C / C | Native CLI is documented. ConPTY, Windows store discovery, file locking, and sandbox mode MUST pass. Windows 11 is the release baseline; Windows 10 is best effort and requires ConPTY. |\n3908|| Claude / macOS | A / C / C | Installed 2.1.229 help confirms UUID resume and unrestricted flag; store transfer remains gated. |\n3909|| Claude / Linux | A / C / C | Provider family documented; distro/PTTY fixture required. |\n3910|| Claude / WSL2 | A / C / C | WSL is provider-documented; use Linux store and path rules. |\n3911|| Claude / native Windows | C / C / C | Windows 10+ with WSL or Git for Windows is documented, but native PowerShell/ConPTY and native store materialization require acceptance. |\n3912|| Gemini / macOS | A / C / C | Official session root, UUID resume, and session-file surface documented. |\n3913|| Gemini / Linux | A / C / C | Ubuntu 20.04+ documented; other distributions conditional. |\n3914|| Gemini / WSL2 | C / C / C | Linux inference; mounted-filesystem, auth, signal, and path-hash tests required. |\n3915|| Gemini / native Windows | A / C / C | Windows 11 24H2+ documented; PowerShell/ConPTY and path-hash tests required. |\n3916|| Muse / macOS arm64 | A for probed 0.1.0 / U / C | Narrow resume probe accepted; current 0.2.1 and full idle/cron fidelity remain unverified. |\n3917|| Muse / macOS amd64 | C / U / C | Artifact/contract exists; not executed. |\n3918|| Muse / Linux amd64 or arm64 | C / U / C | Official launcher artifacts; not executed. |\n3919|| Muse / WSL2 | C / U / ? | Linux-path inference only. |\n3920|| Muse / native Windows | ? / U / ? | 0.2.1 artifacts exist, but official launcher and persistence contract do not establish support. |\n3921|| Antigravity / macOS amd64 or arm64 | C / U / C | Resume works only when the authenticated backend realm resolves the UUID; <code>Stop.fullyIdle</code> is documented. |\n3922|| Antigravity / Linux amd64 or arm64 | C / U / C | Native family documented; keyring/DBus and PTY tests required. |\n3923|| Antigravity / WSL2 | C / U / ? | Linux inference only; auth, path, signal, and locking tests required. |\n3924|| Antigravity / native Windows amd64 or arm64 | C / U / C | Native family documented; ConPTY, data-root expansion, and file-lock tests required. |\n3925|| Pi / macOS | A / C / C | Installed 0.73.1 help verifies session surfaces and default full tool set. |\n3926|| Pi / Linux | C / C / C | Cross-platform Node/package behavior is plausible but exact 0.73.1 acceptance is required. |\n3927|| Pi / WSL2 | C / C / C | Treat as Linux only after path/signal/auth tests. |\n3928|| Pi / native Windows | C / C / C | Provider platform notes exist; exact 0.73.1 store, shell, and ConPTY behavior is unverified. |\n3929|| Qwen task-board prompt mode / any target platform | U direct; A only where task-board probe reports <code>prompt_spawn</code> | No direct native-store or primary-owner claim. |\n3930|| Future plugin / any | ? / ? / ? | Disabled until a tuple-specific probe and acceptance record exist. |\n3931|\n3932|The release MUST NOT collapse WSL2 and native Windows into one row. An adapter\n3933|accepted in WSL2 does not establish native Windows support.\n3934|\n3935|## 9. Task-board integration\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
