code>,\\n353:They remain subject to Section 16's credential, authentication-state, and\\n433:16. The tmux socket and provider authentication state are machine-local\\n484:16. <a id=\\\"dir-inv-16\\\"></a><code>DIR-INV-16</code>: job and continuation\\n723:separate focused PlantUML sources from Sections 4, 10.8, 12, 13, and 16.7. Section\\n832:| Marker <code>sha256:385c71c7a29a43615c9d35ffb7c93ae20cd9419bbca461627048de575cade94c</code> | <code>markers/sha256/38/5c71c7a29a43615c9d35ffb7c93ae20cd9419bbca461627048de575cade94c.json</code> | <code>markers\\\\sha256\\\\38\\\\5c71c7a29a43615c9d35ffb7c93ae20cd9419bbca461627048de575cade94c.json</code> |\\n910:| <code>static_capability_claims</code> | sorted by capability, unique TerminalBackendCapabilityClaim[0..16] whose <code>origin</code> is <code>static</code> |\\n931:| <code>capability_claims</code> | sorted by capability, unique TerminalBackendCapabilityClaim[0..16] |\\n1132:| <code>probe</code> | <code>{platform:macos\\\\|linux\\\\|wsl2\\\\|windows,os_version:string[1..256],requested_capabilities:sorted-unique TerminalBackendCapability[0..16],deadline_at:timestamp}</code> | <code>{probe:TerminalBackendProbe,evidence:sorted-by-evidence_id unique CapabilityEvidence[0..256]}</code> |\\n1186:<dfn>TerminalBackendCapability</dfn> is the exact 16-value registry below.\\n1579:  \\\"record_id\\\": \\\"sha256:0acd3e31635372e176f8f37b1b74aa0ebdcf2d1e4ac40d43adb8e462079b34a2\\\",\\n2162:| <code>kind = git</code> | <code>workspace_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>kind:git</code>, <code>group_relative_path:path</code>, <code>repository_identity:string[1..256]</code>, <code>sanitized_remote_urls:sorted unique sanitized-git-URL[1..16]</code>, <code>repo_relative_cwd:.&#124;path</code>, <code>agent_project_config_paths:sorted unique path[0..256]</code>, <code>materialization_policy:shared_checkout&#124;separate_worktree</code> |\\n2888:| <code>TerminalDescriptor</code> | <code>backend:tmux&#124;conpty</code>, <code>terminal_id:string[1..512]</code>, <code>interactive:boolean</code>, <code>columns:uint16[1..1000]</code>, <code>rows:uint16[1..1000]</code> |\\n3468:| <code>columns</code> / <code>rows</code> | uint16[1..1000] |\\n===\\ninternal/traceability/ownership.v0.5.0.json:2317:        \\\"Session Directory Operation Receipt [urn:ax:schema:session-directory-operation-receipt]\\\",\\ninternal/traceability/ownership.v0.5.0.json:2776:      \\\"gap\\\": \\\"ForRelease only returns the reviewed typed catalog rows that reference 7.3; the RFC 2119 scanner measures no clause line under 7.3, because the closed Provider Manifest states its obligations as a required-member table, a 16-entry operation registry and exactly 7 capability names rather than in uppercase keywords, so the gate cannot measure this section - and no provider manifest is implemented anywhere in this repository.\\\"\\ninternal/traceability/ownership.v0.5.0.json:3295:        \\\"catalog:Appendix D: Directory Node operation body\\\",\\ninternal/traceability/ownership.v0.5.0.json:3297:        \\\"catalog:Appendix D: Directory Query operation/preset\\\",\\ninternal/traceability/ownership.v0.5.0.json:3302:        \\\"catalog:Appendix D: Provider operation body\\\",\\ninternal/traceability/ownership.v0.5.0.json:3305:        \\\"catalog:Appendix D: RPC operation body\\\",\\ninternal/traceability/ownership.v0.5.0.json:3314:        \\\"catalog:Appendix D: Task-board bridge operation\\\",\\ninternal/traceability/ownership.v0.5.0.json:3361:      \\\"gap\\\": \\\"One of the nine Section 14.2 clauses stays unimplemented here. Clause 14.2#6 requires the process exit status to equal the failure object's exit_code. Emit resolves that exact status from the Structured Error registry and returns it, and ExitStatus reports it without emitting, but this repository builds no ax binary: the only os.Exit calls in the tree are the exit(1) failure paths of cataloggen and tracecheck, so no process in this repository ever terminates with a CLI failure status and the process-level half of 14.2#6 is unowned. Read checks the same equality from the consuming side and refuses an invocation whose failure object and observed status disagree, which narrows the gap to the missing process and does not close it. The other eight clauses are discharged - the common flag set, the --yes admission rule, the one-JSON-document boundary, the destructive-operation confirmation and expectation-flag rules, the rpc serve --json refusal, and the takeover adoption rule.\\\",\\ninternal/traceability/ownership.v0.5.0.json:3391:          \\\"excerpt\\\": \\\"Destructive or split-brain-risk operations MUST prompt in interactive mode and\\\",\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 5409,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1353,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
