{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c95d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06ed9-7c63-74b3-b8db-139ac4482e30"},"sequence":777,"recorded_at":1780531400001549,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"680c30af-893a-4c96-ab8b-878d612e53c6","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"680c30af-893a-4c96-ab8b-878d612e53c6","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"680c30af-893a-4c96-ab8b-878d612e53c6"},"call_id":"call_01a06edb23e67c21b67fc391fcda8c4f","text":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.md`.\n(10961 line(s) above)\n10962|## 15. Errors and exit semantics\n10963|\n10964|### 15.1 Structured Error\n10965|\n10966|All machine-readable errors use <code>urn:ax:schema:error</code>. Existing\n10967|Provider/RPC/Bridge and legacy CLI surfaces select version <code>1.0.0</code>,\n10968|whose exact shape is:\n10969|\n10970|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n10971|| --- | --- | --- |\n10972|| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact Structured Error schema identifier |\n10973|| <code>schema_version</code> | semver | Exact <code>1.0.0</code> |\n10974|| <code>code</code> | string[1..128] | Stable lower-snake-case registry value |\n10975|| <code>message</code> | string[1..4096] | Human text; automation does not branch on it |\n10976|| <code>exit_code</code> | int32 | Exact Section 15.2 code assigned to <code>code</code> |\n10977|| <code>retryable</code> | boolean | True only when the identical request may safely be retried without new authority or confirmation |\n10978|| <code>operation_id</code> | UUIDv7, optional | Present whenever an operation was allocated |\n10979|| <code>session_id</code> | UUIDv7, optional | Present whenever the failure is session-scoped |\n10980|| <code>details</code> | diagnostic data map | Required, redacted open map constrained below |\n10981|\n10982|~~~json\n10983|{\n10984|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:error\",\n10985|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n10986|  \"code\": \"workspace_conflict\",\n10987|  \"message\": \"destination differs from its last materialized checkpoint\",\n10988|  \"exit_code\": 5,\n10989|  \"retryable\": false,\n10990|  \"operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-b180-7299-9273-1234567890ab\",\n10991|  \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n10992|  \"details\": {\n10993|    \"expected_checkpoint\": \"sha256:2222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222222\",\n10994|    \"remediations\": [\"diff\", \"copy\", \"worktree\", \"replace_managed_replica\"]\n10995|  }\n10996|}\n10997|~~~\n10998|\n10999|<code>schema</code>, <code>schema_version</code>, <code>code</code>,\n11000|<code>message</code>, <code>exit_code</code>, <code>retryable</code>, and\n11001|<code>details</code> are required. Operation and session IDs are optional and\n11002|MUST be present when known. Messages are for humans; automation MUST branch on\n11003|<code>code</code> and <code>exit_code</code>. Details MUST be redacted and\n11004|schema-valid.\n11005|\n11006|The top-level object is closed. <code>message</code> is 1–4,096 UTF-8\n11007|characters. <code>details</code> is an explicitly open diagnostic data map, not\n11008|an implicit schema extension: it has 0–64 keys matching\n11009|<code>[a-z][a-z0-9_]{0,63}</code>, JSON values of maximum nesting depth 4, and\n11010|maximum canonical size 16 KiB. Readers MAY ignore unknown detail keys and MUST\n11011|never infer success, authority, or a remediation action from them. No detail\n11012|may contain a credential, raw transcript, environment secret, or opaque bundle\n11013|content.\n11014|\n11015|Structured Error is independently versioned as a reusable schema, but that\n11016|does not imply independent negotiation inside every envelope. Provider\n11017|protocol <code>2.x</code>, task-board bridge <code>1.x</code>, and Mesh RPC\n11018|<code>2.x</code> each embed exactly Structured Error <code>1.0.0</code>. A\n11019|supported-major failure MUST use that exact object; the containing protocol\n11020|version is sufficient to select it. RPC hello MUST NOT advertise or negotiate\n11021|an <code>error</code> contract key. A future containing-protocol version may\n11022|bind another error version only by stating the new binding explicitly.\n11023|\n11024|Session Adapter 1.0 and <code>session.clone.*</code> bind Structured Error\n11025|1.1.0. It retains the 1.0.0 shape and codes, changes only\n11026|<code>schema_version</code> to exact <code>1.1.0</code>, and adds:\n11027|\n11028|| Exit | Stable clone codes |\n11029|| ---: | --- |\n11030|| 4 | <code>source_not_found</code>, <code>source_ambiguous</code> |\n11031|| 6 | <code>unsupported_environment_tuple</code>, <code>operation_unknown</code>, <code>target_resume_invalid</code> |\n11032|| 9 | <code>source_corrupt</code>, <code>bundle_integrity_failed</code>, <code>credential_material_detected</code> |\n11033|| 11 | <code>source_not_quiescent</code>, <code>source_changed_during_clone</code> |\n11034|| 12 | <code>target_prepare_failed</code>, <code>target_validation_failed</code>, <code>target_checkpoint_failed</code>, <code>transaction_unknown</code> |\n11035|| 13 | <code>session_adapter_protocol_error</code>, <code>session_adapter_process_failed</code>, <code>session_adapter_timeout</code> |\n11036|| 16 | <code>projection_loss_unacceptable</code>, <code>unsafe_pending_action</code> |\n11037|\n11038|Existing semantically identical codes remain reused. Transaction unknown is a\n11039|parked ambiguous effect, never success or absence. Target checkpoint failure\n11040|occurs only after Provider commit and grants no rollback; the exact inert target\n11041|remains recoverable.\n11042|\n11043|Bootstrap and incompatible-major behavior is exact:\n11044|\n11045|| Surface | Supported-major failure before normal success | Unsupported major or unparseable first frame/output |\n11046|| --- | --- | --- |\n11047|| Provider JSON-over-stdio | A syntactically valid v2 request whose operation/body fails receives the Section 7.2 v2 failure envelope with Error 1.0.0 | The plugin MUST NOT masquerade a different-major object as v2. The host accepts no child error object, terminates/waits for exit as applicable, and emits its own local Error 1.0.0: <code>incompatible_protocol</code> for a recognizable major mismatch, otherwise <code>provider_protocol_error</code> |\n11048|| Task-board bridge facade | A syntactically valid v1 invocation failure receives the Section 9.2 v1 failure envelope with Error 1.0.0 | The facade output is not accepted as a bridge result. <code>ax</code> emits its own local Error 1.0.0: <code>incompatible_protocol</code> for a recognizable major mismatch, otherwise <code>task_board_bridge_unavailable</code> |\n11049|| Mesh RPC | Before hello success, a syntactically valid v2 non-hello request or invalid v2 hello receives one v2 failure envelope with Error 1.0.0 and the server then closes | An unsupported protocol major, invalid JSON, oversize line, missing protocol/version/request ID, or response that cannot be framed causes close without an RPC error frame. The initiator emits its own local Error 1.0.0: <code>incompatible_protocol</code> for a recognizable major mismatch, otherwise <code>transport_failure</code> |\n11050|\n11051|A local error above is an <code>ax</code> CLI/observation result, not a forged\n11052|response attributed to the child or peer; it omits unknown operation/session\n11053|IDs and records redacted diagnostics only. Receivers MUST NOT parse a different\n11054|major's payload far enough to trust its error code, retryable bit, details, or\n11055|authority fields.\n11056|\n11057|The normative binding fixtures are\n11058|<code>ERR-PROVIDER-COMPAT</code>, <code>ERR-BRIDGE-COMPAT</code>, and\n11059|<code>ERR-RPC-COMPAT</code>, which use the documented provider/RPC v2 and bridge\n11060|v1 failure envelopes; <code>ERR-PROVIDER-MAJOR</code>,\n11061|<code>ERR-BRIDGE-MAJOR</code>, and <code>ERR-RPC-MAJOR</code>, which change only\n11062|the containing protocol major to 3 for provider/RPC or 2 for the bridge and require the local\n11063|<code>incompatible_protocol</code> result; and\n11064|<code>ERR-PROVIDER-FIRST</code>, <code>ERR-BRIDGE-FIRST</code>, and\n11065|<code>ERR-RPC-FIRST</code>. Provider and RPC fixtures submit valid v2 envelopes\n11066|with an invalid first operation/body and require the bound v2 error; the bridge\n11067|fixture uses its valid v1 invocation and bound v1 error. The RPC fixture submits\n11068|<code>health.get</code> before hello, requires one bound v2 error, and then EOF.\n11069|<code>ERR-FIRST-UNFRAMED</code> supplies invalid JSON to\n11070|each stdio parser (or invalid JSON output from the bridge) and requires no\n11071|remote/child error to be trusted.\n11072|\n11073|### 15.2 Exit codes\n11074|\n11075|| Exit | Meaning |\n11076|| ---: | --- |\n11077|| 0 | Requested operation succeeded |\n11078|| 2 | Usage, invalid flag, or interactive choice required |\n11079|| 3 | Configuration or local precondition invalid |\n11080|| 4 | Session, checkpoint, peer, provider, or task-board identity not found |\n11081|| 5 | Workspace/native-store conflict; no silent overwrite |\n11082|| 6 | Capability unsupported, unknown, conditional, or incompatible |\n11083|| 7 | Authentication/authorization/allowlist failure |\n11084|| 8 | SSH/RPC transport failure; staging can be resumable |\n11085|| 9 | Integrity, schema, hash, or unsafe-path failure |\n11086|| 10 | Ownership/lease/fencing failure |\n11087|| 11 | Busy, quiesce timeout, or graceful stop timeout |\n11088|| 12 | Staging/materialization/rollback failure |\n11089|| 13 | Provider plugin/process failure |\n11090|| 14 | Task-board bridge/bundle/validation failure |\n11091|| 15 | Partial success: immutable sync succeeded but a requested materialization or peer did not |\n11092|| 16 | Explicit policy refusal, including missing destructive confirmation |\n11093|| 17 | Contract/schema migration required |\n11094|| 130 | Interrupted by operator signal before a clean response; inspect authority before retry |\n11095|\n11096|### 15.3 Stable error codes\n11097|\n11098|Protocol 1.0.0 fixes these code-to-exit mappings:\n11099|\n11100|| Exit | Stable error codes |\n11101|| ---: | --- |\n11102|| 2 | <code>interactive_choice_required</code>, <code>invalid_arguments</code> |\n11103|| 3 | <code>invalid_config</code>, <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code> |\n11104|| 4 | <code>name_ambiguous</code>, <code>not_found</code> |\n11105|| 5 | <code>workspace_conflict</code>, <code>native_store_conflict</code> |\n11106|| 6 | <code>capability_unavailable</code>, <code>profile_mapping_unavailable</code>, <code>incompatible_protocol</code>, <code>incompatible_schema</code>, <code>provider_fork_unsupported</code>, <code>unsupported_backend_identity</code> |\n11107|| 7 | <code>authentication_failed</code>, <code>peer_not_allowlisted</code>, <code>host_identity_mismatch</code> |\n11108|| 8 | <code>owner_unreachable</code>, <code>transport_failure</code> |\n11109|| 9 | <code>unsafe_path</code>, <code>integrity_failure</code> |\n11110|| 10 | <code>not_owner</code>, <code>stale_owner</code>, <code>lease_conflict</code>, <code>invalid_state_transition</code> |\n11111|| 11 | <code>quiesce_timeout</code>, <code>stop_timeout</code>, <code>workspace_group_busy</code>, <code>workspace_group_changed</code> |\n11112|| 12 | <code>staging_incomplete</code>, <code>atomic_commit_unavailable</code>, <code>materialization_failed</code>, <code>rollback_failed</code> |\n11113|| 13 | <code>provider_timeout</code>, <code>provider_protocol_error</code>, <code>provider_process_failed</code> |\n11114|| 14 | <code>task_board_bridge_unavailable</code>, <code>task_board_bundle_invalid</code>, <code>task_board_validate_failed</code>, <code>checkpoint_unavailable</code> |\n11115|| 15 | <code>partial_sync</code> |\n11116|| 16 | <code>confirmation_required</code>, <code>policy_refused</code>, <code>secret_policy_violation</code> |\n11117|| 17 | <code>migration_required</code> |\n11118|| 130 | <code>interrupted</code> |\n11119|\n11120|New error codes MAY be added in a compatible minor contract version, but an\n11121|unknown code retains the envelope's exit class and MUST NOT be interpreted as\n11122|success.\n11123|\n11124|The v0.4.3 realm and route constraints add no error code. Missing or unsafe\n11125|broker/server-generation/functional-sentinel evidence uses\n11126|<code>capability_unavailable</code> with typed details containing\n11127|<code>capability</code>, <code>caller_realm</code>,\n11128|<code>broker_state</code>, <code>tmux_server_generation</code>, and\n11129|<code>remediation</code>. A missing or failed provider-auth smoke uses\n11130|<code>target_auth_missing</code> with typed <code>provider_id</code>,\n11131|<code>provider_build</code>, <code>macos_version</code>,\n11132|<code>tmux_server_generation</code>, and <code>remediation</code>. Route choice\n11133|continues to use <code>interactive_choice_required</code>. Implementations MUST\n11134|NOT mint a realm-specific code while these existing codes remain truthful.\n11135|\n11136|Structured Error 1.2.0 retains the exact 1.1 shape and all prior codes. It is\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
