{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000e337","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06ed9-7c63-74b3-b8db-139ac4482e30"},"sequence":4086,"recorded_at":1780531400008167,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"680c30af-893a-4c96-ab8b-878d612e53c6","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"680c30af-893a-4c96-ab8b-878d612e53c6","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"680c30af-893a-4c96-ab8b-878d612e53c6"},"terminal":"completed","text":"Ready for review — handed off to review as `to-review` with 10/10 checklist and three outcome artifacts.\n\nWhat was built: new `internal/provhost` package implementing the §7.2 JSONL host transport (one-frame envelopes, 8 MiB limits, UTF-8/duplicate/closed-member decoding, stdout/stderr separation with redaction), deadline enforcement with process-group kill, dispatch over exactly the 15 §7.5 operations derived from the pinned table, and fail-closed status recovery (`unknown` → `integrity_failure` quarantine, evolving reads, fresh process per call). Local failures are `*axerror.Error` through six audited constructors; child failures via the static provider-major-2 binding.\n\nAlso closed: F18 (attester pin, SEAM1 verified red), F19 (planted candidates, partial-set mutant reddens), F20 (`GOOS=windows go vet` CI step, verified against a planted type error). Left uncommitted per the CR shape.\n\nEvidence: full suite 15/15 exit 0, `-race` exit 0 in batches, both-platform `vet` exit 0, `gofmt`/`tracecheck`/catalog clean, provhost cover 86.1% with stated bound, 25/25 narrowing mutants killed with verified presence and restores. One correction worth knowing: the registry counts 15, not 16 — the ownership gap prose miscounts; both the manifest and §7.5 table list 15, and the test derives them in order.","reason":null}}
